ns","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3944554708","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/635#issuecomment-3944554708","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/635","id":3944554708,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7rHSDU","user":{"login":"nonameffh","id":5434885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzQ4ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5434885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh","html_url":"https://github.com/nonameffh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T12:44:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T12:44:17Z","body":"### New Requirements Added\r\n\r\n| ID | Priority | Name | Description |\r\n|----|----------|------|-------------|\r\n| `cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-file-type-classification` | p1 | File Type Classification (GTS) | Mandatory GTS file type identifier on every file at upload time for per-actor, per-module access control isolation |\r\n| `cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-backend-capabilities` | p1 | Backend Capabilities | Formal capability model (presigned URLs, versioning, multipart upload, server-side encryption) — declared, independently configurable, runtime-discoverable |\r\n| `cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-conditional-requests` | p1 | Conditional Requests (ETags) | ETag headers, `If-None-Match` for cache validation, `If-Match` for concurrent update protection (RFC 7232) |\r\n| `cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-file-versioning` | p2 | File Versioning | Version creation on upload, retrieval/listing/soft-delete/permanent-delete by opaque version ID; requires versioning backend capability |\r\n| `cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-owner-deletion` | p2 | Owner Deletion Handling | Consume owner deletion events from EventBroker, execute configurable Serverless Runtime workflow for file disposition |\r\n| `cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-usage-reporting` | p2 | Storage Usage Reporting | Asynchronous per-tenant usage reports to Usage Collector on every storage-changing write operation |\r\n| `cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-upload-idempotency` | p2 | Upload Idempotency | Client-provided idempotency keys for safe upload retries |\r\n| `cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-file-encryption` | p3 | File Encryption | Server-side encryption at rest, requires encryption backend capability |\r\n| `cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-read-audit` | p3 | Read Audit Logging | Optional per-policy audit logging for read operations passing through FileStorage |\r\n| `cpt-cf-file-storage-nfr-scalability` | p1 | Scalability & Capacity | ≥1,000 concurrent operations per instance; linear horizontal scaling |\r\n\r\n### Priority Changes\r\n\r\n| Requirement | Old | New | Rationale |\r\n|-------------|-----|-----|-----------|\r\n| Shareable Links (`fr-shareable-links`) | p1 | p2 | Sharing is not core phase 1 |\r\n| Link Expiration (`fr-link-expiration`) | p1 | p2 | Follows shareable links priority |\r\n| Manage Links (`fr-manage-links`) | p1 | p2 | Follows shareable links priority |\r\n| Audit Trail (`fr-audit-trail`) | p1 | p2 | Audit infrastructure is a p2 dependency |\r\n| Audit Completeness (`nfr-audit-completeness`) | p1 | p2 | Aligns with audit trail priority |\r\n| Upload and Share use case | p1 | p2 | Follows shareable links priority |\r\n| Manage Links use case | p1 | p2 | Follows manage links priority |\r\n\r\n### Scope Changes\r\n\r\n**Moved from Out of Scope to In Scope (previously it phase meant like phase 2,3,4):**\r\n- S3-compatible API, WebDAV API, Streaming and range requests\r\n- Runtime tenant-configurable storage backends\r\n- Storage quota enforcement, Ownership transfer, Custom metadata limits\r\n- File versioning (was explicitly out of scope)\r\n- Conditional requests (ETags), Upload idempotency\r\n- Owner deletion handling via EventBroker and Serverless Runtime\r\n- File encryption\r\n\r\n### GTS File Type Integration (Cross-Cutting)\r\n\r\nAdded GTS file type as a cross-cutting concern throughout the PRD:\r\n- New mandatory field in metadata storage and all metadata responses\r\n- Authorization requests now include GTS type in resource context for per-type access decisions\r\n- Upload flows require GTS file type (validation step added to upload and direct upload use cases)\r\n- GTS file type is immutable after creation\r\n- Added to system-managed metadata list (not user-updatable)\r\n- New acceptance criteria for type-based access isolation between modules\r\n\r\n### Terminology & Model Changes\r\n\r\n| Before | After | Reason |\r\n|--------|-------|--------|\r\n| \"Tenant Policy\" | \"Policy\" | Policies now apply at both tenant and user levels; most restrictive wins |\r\n| \"Webhook Triggers\" (`fr-webhook-triggers`) | \"File Events\" (`fr-file-events`) | Events emitted to EventBroker, not direct webhooks |\r\n| \"tenants\" (as policy definers) | \"owners\" | Consistent with dual-level policy model |\r\n| \"Tenant-scoped access control\" | \"Tenant-scoped and origin-module-scoped access control\" | Reflects module ownership model |\r\n| Authorization Service as system actor | Removed from actors | It's a dependency, not an actor |\r\n\r\n### Behavior Changes\r\n\r\n**Signed URLs:**\r\n- Removed \"short expiration\" mandate; replaced with dual-source expiration model (backend limit ceiling + policy limits, most restrictive wins)\r\n- Removed fallback to proxied serving for unsupported backends → now rejects with clear error\r\n- Now explicitly requires presigned URLs backend capability\r\n\r\n**Direct Transfer URLs:**\r\n- Changed from bidirectional (upload + download) to upload-only; downloads covered by signed URLs\r\n- Removed fallback to proxied transfer → now rejects with clear error when capability unavailable\r\n- Added abandoned upload alternative flow referencing GC requirement\r\n\r\n**Multipart Upload:**\r\n- Now requires multipart upload backend capability\r\n- Added explicit rejection behavior for backends without native multipart support (no FileStorage-level fallback)\r\n\r\n**File Ownership:**\r\n- Changed from \"immutable after creation\" to \"immutable except through explicit ownership transfer or owner deletion workflows\"\r\n\r\n**List Files:**\r\n- Additional filters changed from SHOULD to MUST\r\n\r\n**Garbage Collection:**\r\n- Rewritten with presigned URL expiration + configurable grace period as eligibility window\r\n- Added reconciliation: confirm records whose backend object exists but was never acknowledged\r\n\r\n**File Size Limits:**\r\n- Added backend limit as hard ceiling that no policy can override\r\n- Most-restrictive-wins model across tenant and user policy levels\r\n\r\n**Storage Quota:**\r\n- Simplified to pre-upload check with Quota Enforcement service\r\n- Scope expanded from tenant-only to owner (tenant or user)\r\n\r\n**Delete File use case:**\r\n- Simplified: revokes shareable links only (signed URLs are non-revocable by nature)\r\n\r\n**Audit in use cases:**\r\n- Audit record emission deferred to Phase 2 in: signed URL generation, direct upload, file deletion","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3944554708/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"con