are still missing from the document.**\n\nThe document extensively uses \"Phase 1\" and \"Phase 2\" throughout — in requirement priorities (`p1`/`p2`), inline annotations (`*(Phase 2)*`), use case steps, section titles (`### 5.5 Policies (Phase 2)`), and the Success Metrics table. Yet there is no formal definition of what these phases constitute. A reader cannot determine which requirements are in scope for the initial release without this context.\n\nAdd a dedicated \"Phases\" subsection (under §4 Scope or as a standalone §1.x) that defines:\n- What Phase 1 and Phase 2 include\n- Delivery milestones / timeframes for each phase\n- Acceptance criteria for phase transition\n- Mapping to the Success Metrics timeframes in §1.4\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/file-storage/docs/PRD.md` around lines 94 - 128, Add a new \"Phases\"\nsubsection under \"### 4. Scope\" that explicitly defines Phase 1 and Phase 2\n(what features and requirements belong to each, e.g., Phase 1 = core\nupload/download/list/delete, auth, basic metadata, signed URLs; Phase 2 =\npolicies, sharing hierarchy, advanced backends, versioning), include delivery\nmilestones/timeframes for each phase, state clear acceptance criteria for\ntransitioning from Phase 1 to Phase 2 (e.g., test coverage, performance targets,\ncritical success metrics), and map these phase timeframes to the Success Metrics\nreferences in §1.4 and any inline Phase annotations like \"### 5.5 Policies\n(Phase 2)\" so readers can unambiguously determine what is in the initial release\nversus later work.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@modules/file-storage/docs/PRD.md`:\n- Line 1036: In the PRD use cases, the audit-emission steps for Phase 2 are\nmissing the annotation: update the three occurrences by prepending \"*(Phase 2)*\n\" to the step texts \"FileStorage emits audit record for the upload\" (Upload and\nShare a File), \"FileStorage emits audit record for the link revocation\" (Manage\nShareable Links), and \"audit record emitted for link creation\" (Manage Shareable\nLinks alt flow); also change the Manage Shareable Links postcondition \"- Audit\nrecord emitted\" to \"- *(Phase 2)* Audit record emitted\" so all audit steps\nconsistently indicate Phase 2.\n- Around line 1307-1358: The Acceptance Criteria section is missing testable\nitems for several p2/p3 requirements; add explicit criteria for each listed\nrequirement ID (e.g., cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-storage-quota,\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-usage-reporting, cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-file-events,\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-range-requests, cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-s3-api,\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-webdav-api, cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-retention-policies,\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-sharing-restrictions,\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-runtime-backends,\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-ownership-transfer,\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-metadata-limits, cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-read-audit) by\ninserting short, testable acceptance criteria mirroring the behavior described\nin §5 (e.g., \"Upload rejected when storage quota would be exceeded\" for\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-storage-quota, \"Usage report emitted asynchronously on\nstorage-consuming write operations\" for cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-usage-reporting,\n\"Read audit records emitted for proxied downloads when enabled; not emitted for\npresigned URL downloads\" for cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-read-audit, and equivalent\nsingle-line criteria for each remaining ID) ensuring wording matches other\nchecklist items and uses consistent phrasing and priority labels.\n- Around line 1230-1237: Update the \"Manage Shareable Links\" main flow to\ninclude an explicit authorization check as step 2 (mirroring other use cases):\nafter \"Owner requests the list of all active shareable links...\" insert\n\"FileStorage calls Authorization Service to verify the owner's permission to\nlist/manage shareable links\" before returning the list, and ensure the\nrevocation path similarly documents an Authorization Service call prior to\ninvalidation; reference the \"Manage Shareable Links\" flow, FileStorage, and\nAuthorization Service when making the change.\n- Around line 1206-1211: The postcondition \"All associated links invalidated\"\nconflicts with the signed URL non-revocability requirements; update the\npostcondition text to explicitly limit invalidation to shareable/manageable\nlinks only (e.g., \"All associated shareable/manageable links invalidated; signed\nURLs remain valid\") and reference the related requirements\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-delete-file, cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-signed-urls, and\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-manage-links to ensure the wording aligns with the\nnon-revocability design.\n- Around line 38-44: Update the Success Metrics table row for \"Audit coverage\nfor file write operations\" in PRD.md: replace the non-calendar timeframe \"Phase\n2\" with a concrete calendar-relative timeframe (e.g., \"9 months after GA\" or\nanother agreed-upon date relative to GA/module adoption) so the delivery window\nis resolvable; if the exact duration is undecided, insert a temporary\ncalendar-relative placeholder and add an action item for owners to finalize it\nwhen phase definitions are available.\n\n---\n\nDuplicate comments:\nIn `@modules/file-storage/docs/PRD.md`:\n- Around line 94-128: Add a new \"Phases\" subsection under \"### 4. Scope\" that\nexplicitly defines Phase 1 and Phase 2 (what features and requirements belong to\neach, e.g., Phase 1 = core upload/download/list/delete, auth, basic metadata,\nsigned URLs; Phase 2 = policies, sharing hierarchy, advanced backends,\nversioning), include delivery milestones/timeframes for each phase, state clear\nacceptance criteria for transitioning from Phase 1 to Phase 2 (e.g., test\ncoverage, performance targets, critical success metrics), and map these phase\ntimeframes to the Success Metrics references in §1.4 and any inline Phase\nannotations like \"### 5.5 Policies (Phase 2)\" so readers can unambiguously\ndetermine what is in the initial release versus later work.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 151b1979fdfc0611b945b1c34160d3f46b88d7e6 and 75f6fd009fea8f95fc17d533e9f2170a4edd68f7.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (1)</summary>\n\n* `modules/file-storage/docs/PRD.md`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/635#pullrequestreview-3840917307","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/635","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/635#pullrequestreview-3840917307"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/635"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-23T12:56:01Z","commit_id":"75f6fd009fea8f95fc17d533e9f2170a4edd68f7"},{"id":3841022586,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7k8Vp6","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 5**\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/file-storage/docs/PRD.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`94-133`: **Phase definitions still absent from the document.**\n\nA dedicated section formally defining Phase 1 and Phase 2 (scope, milestones, acceptance gates, mapping to 1.4 Success Metrics) was requested in a previous review cycle and the author acknowledged it. The current document still only carries inline `*(Phase 2)*` annotations and the `### 5.5 Policies (Phase 2)` heading — no formal definition exists.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/file-storage/docs/PRD.md` around lines 94 - 133, The document lacks a\nformal \"Phases\" section defining Phase 1 and Phase 2 despite inline “*(Phase\n2)*” tags and the heading \"### 5.5 Policies (Phase 2)\"; add a new section (e.g.,\n\"4.x Phases\" or \"5.x Phases\") that explicitly defines Phase 1 and Phase 2 with\ntheir scope, milestones, acceptance gates, and how each maps to \"1.4 Success\nMetrics\", and update references (remove ambiguous inline annotations and ensure\n\"### 5.5 Policies (Phase 2)\" clearly links to the Phase definitions) so\nreviewers can unambiguously see which features belong to which phase and what\ncriteria mark completion.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`199-234`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify content-type validation applicability and timing for multipart uploads.**\n\n`cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-content-type-validation` (line 225) scopes validation to \"proxied uploads (where file content passes through FileStorage).\" Multipart upload (lines 203-213) is a proxied operation (chunks pass through FileStorage), but the requirement is silent on:\n\n- Whether validation runs per-part, on the first part only, or on the fully assembled file.\n- What happens if the backend performs server-side assembly after receiving individual parts — FileStorage may not have a contiguous content stream to inspect.\n\nWithout this clarification, implementors could skip content-type validation for multipart uploads entirely, defeating the security guarantee for large files.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested addition to <code>cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-content-type-validation</code></summary>\n\n```diff\n Content-type validation does not apply to direct uploads via presigned URLs because\n FileStorage does not receive the file content in that flow.\n+\n+For multipart uploads, content-type validation **MUST** be applied. Validation **MUST**\n+be performed against the leading bytes (magic bytes/file signature) of the first uploaded\n+part, which are sufficient to determine the actual content type. Parts subsequent to the\n+first are not re-validated independently.\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/file-storage/docs/PRD.md` around lines 199 - 234, Update the\ncontent-type validation requirement\n(cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-content-type-validation) to explicitly cover proxied\nmultipart uploads (cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-multipart-upload): require FileStorage\nto perform lightweight per-part signature checks on each uploaded part and a\nfinal full-file validation after assembly when FileStorage assembles parts\nitself; if only per-part checks are possible (e.g., backend performs server-side\nassembly), require FileStorage to validate the first N parts and abort with a\nclear error if any part's detected type conflicts with the declared mime_type\nand additionally require the backend to report assembly completion so\nFileStorage can perform a final validation or mark the upload as unverifiable\nand reject it—document the exact failure modes and error messages for per-part\nmismatch, deferred backend assembly, and unverifiable assemblies.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@modules/file-storage/docs/PRD.md`:\n- Around line 530-539: Update the quota requirement\n`cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-storage-quota` to include version creation and any other\nstorage-consuming write operations (not just \"uploads\") in its pre-check scope:\nexplicitly state that before accepting uploads or actions that create new file\nversions (or otherwise increase stored bytes) the system MUST consult the Quota\nEnforcement service and reject operations that would exceed the owner's quota;\nmirror the terminology used in `cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-usage-reporting` so\nversion creation is handled consistently.\n- Line 56: Update the \"Signed URL\" glossary entry to note that while the URL\nsignature itself is non-revocable, deletion of the underlying file/content will\ncause the storage backend to return a 404 (or equivalent) for that signed URL;\nexplicitly mention this edge case and add a cross-reference to the existing\nuse-case postconditions that document the same behavior so readers are not\nsurprised.\n- Around line 836-846: The PRD's idempotency requirement\n(cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-upload-idempotency) lacks key scoping and risks\ncross-caller collisions; update the requirement text to specify the idempotency\nkey scope (e.g., scoped per-tenant and optionally per-user/session) and state\nthat the server MUST namespace keys by tenant_id (and user_id when applicable),\nenforce isolation in the idempotency lookup, and expire keys after the\nconfigurable window; reference the requirement id\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-upload-idempotency and amend associated acceptance\ncriteria and actor descriptions to reflect per-tenant/per-user scoping and\nconfidentiality guarantees.\n- Around line 517-528: Update the usage reporting requirement\n(cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-usage-reporting) to also mandate emitting asynchronous,\nnon-blocking usage updates on ownership transfer events\n(cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-ownership-transfer), explicitly stating that transfers\nmust produce a debit for the previous owner and a credit for the new owner so\nper-owner consumption remains accurate for billing/quota; ensure the wording\npreserves the existing async/non-blocking constraint and that reports include\nper-tenant/per-owner total bytes and file counts.\n- Around line 644-668: Clarify the \"soft-delete\" semantics in the File\nVersioning section (cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-file-versioning) by explicitly\nstating whether a soft-delete is logical-only (marks the current version\ninaccessible while the backend object is physically retained) or physical\n(backend object removed), and list the implications: whether retained data\ncounts against storage quota, whether the GC worker\n(cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-gc-direct-uploads) must consider soft-deleted content\nfor cleanup, and whether undelete/recovery of the current version is supported;\nupdate the wording around \"becomes inaccessible\" to include these outcomes and\nthe required tenant, audit, and authorization behavior for retained vs. removed\nobjects.\n\n---\n\nDuplicate comments:\nIn `@modules/file-storage/docs/PRD.md`:\n- Around line 94-133: The document lacks a formal \"Phases\" section defining\nPhase 1 and Phase 2 despite inline “*(Phase 2)*” tags and the heading \"### 5.5\nPolicies (Phase 2)\"; add a new section (e.g., \"4.x Phases\" or \"5.x Phases\") that\nexplicitly defines Phase 1 and Phase 2 with their scope, milestones, acceptance\ngates, and how each maps to \"1.4 Success Metrics\", and update references (remove\nambiguous inline annotations and ensure \"### 5.5 Policies (Phase 2)\" clearly\nlinks to the Phase definitions) so reviewers can unambiguously see which\nfeatures belong to which phase and what criteria mark completion.\n- Around line 199-234: Update the content-type validation requirement\n(cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-content-type-validation) to explicitly cover proxied\nmultipart uploads (cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-multipart-upload): require FileStorage\nto perform lightweight per-part signature checks on each uploaded part and a\nfinal full-file validation after assembly when FileStorage assembles parts\nitself; if only per-part checks are possible (e.g., backend performs server-side\nassembly), require FileStorage to validate the first N parts and abort with a\nclear error if any part's detected type conflicts with the declared mime_type\nand additionally require the backend to report assembly completion so\nFileStorage can perform a final validation or mark the upload as unverifiable\nand reject it—document the exact failure modes and error messages for per-part\nmismatch, deferred backend assembly, and unverifiable assemblies.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 75f6fd009fea8f95fc17d533e9f2170a4edd68f7 and a019023ceaa441c3c4aed7ba421b66787016584b.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (1)</summary>\n\n* `modules/file-storage/docs/PRD.md`\n\n</details>\n\n</detai