ge/docs/PRD.md`:\n- Around line 229-233: The multipart-upload flow\n(cpt-cf-file-storage-fr-multipart-upload) currently assumes the first part\ncontains enough signature bytes to validate mime_type; modify the upload handler\nthat processes the first part (e.g., the FileStorage method that accepts\nmultipart parts / acceptMultipartPart or handleMultipartPart) to either enforce\na minimum first-part size or buffer incoming data until enough leading bytes are\naccumulated to classify the file’s magic bytes, perform the mime_type validation\nas soon as enough bytes are available, and if validation fails call the\nmultipart abort routine (abortMultipartUpload) and reject/ignore all subsequent\nparts; ensure the logic distinguishes “first part not yet sufficient” (buffer\nand delay accepting later parts) versus “validated and accept” so downstream\nparts are not processed prematurely.\n- Around line 672-679: The PRD currently defines conflicting semantics for\ndeleting versioned files vs the base \"Delete File\" flow (see references to\nDelete File, the \"Delete a File\" use case, and requirement\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-delete-file); pick and document one explicit contract:\neither (A) make the base Delete File operation soft-delete for versioned objects\nand state that permanent deletion requires a separate operation, or (B) add a\ndeleteMode parameter (e.g., \"soft\" | \"permanent\") to the Delete File API and\ndescribe authorization, quota impact, and behavior for current vs non-current\nversions; update all relevant sections to consistently state which API/parameter\nto call for permanent removal, the required auth (same as upload for restore),\nand that soft-deleted data still counts against\ncpt-cf-file-storage-fr-storage-quota.\n- Around line 1397-1403: Update the acceptance checklist to include two\nowner-scoping checks: (1) add an item that \"Retried upload with the same\nidempotency key by a different owner does not return or create the original\nowner's file\" to assert idempotency keys are isolated per owner; and (2) add an\nitem that \"Ownership transfer emits usage reports for both previous and new\nowner\" to ensure the transfer path triggers usage emission for both parties;\nplace these items alongside the existing retry and usage criteria in the same\nchecklist block so testers can verify these security-sensitive behaviors.\n- Around line 1018-1032: The Usage Collector (ID:\ncpt-cf-file-storage-contract-usage-collector) and Quota Enforcement (ID:\ncpt-cf-file-storage-contract-quota-enforcement) contract descriptions must be\nupdated from “per-tenant” to per-owner semantics: change the Protocol/Format for\nUsage Collector to “Asynchronous per-owner usage reports” including explicit\nowner identifiers (owner_id and owner_type: user|tenant) and ownership metadata,\nand change Quota Enforcement to “Synchronous per-owner quota check requests”\nthat accept owner_id/owner_type and consent to ownership-transfer accounting;\nalso update the Compatibility notes to reference owner-based semantics in §5.5.\nApply the same owner-based wording to the other occurrence of these contracts in\nthe document.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n**Run ID**: `468b4a77-74cf-487b-a42a-ba3995e4a02d`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between a019023ceaa441c3c4aed7ba421b66787016584b and 8752e4620d5f1970a7abb0c3e4ec056083478d68.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (1)</summary>\n\n* `modules/file-storage/docs/PRD.md`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/635#pullrequestreview-3909221215","pull_request_url"