ocumentation: a PRD, a comprehensive DESIGN, and three ADRs defining llm_provider as an embedded library, internal transport as HTTP with SSE passthrough, and tenant-owned group-chat usage attribution (documentation-only; no code/public API changes).\n\n## Changes\n\n|Cohort / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**ADRs** <br> `modules/mini-chat/docs/ADR/0001-cpt-cf-mini-chat-adr-llm-provider-as-library.md`, `modules/mini-chat/docs/ADR/0002-cpt-cf-mini-chat-adr-internal-transport.md`, `modules/mini-chat/docs/ADR/0003-cpt-cf-mini-chat-adr-group-chat-usage-attribution.md`|Three new ADRs: choose embedding `llm_provider` as a library crate in chat_service; select HTTP with SSE passthrough for internal transport to OAGW; define tenant-owned group-chat resources with per-request usage attribution.|\n|**Design & PRD** <br> `modules/mini-chat/docs/DESIGN.md`, `modules/mini-chat/docs/PRD.md`|Add full Mini Chat design and product requirements: architecture, API and streaming contracts (REST/SSE), provider mappings, auth/quota model, data lifecycle, observability, and acceptance/operational guidance. Documentation-only additions.|\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant Client as Client\n  participant OAGW as Outbound_API_Gateway\n  participant LLM as llm_provider_lib\n  participant Provider as External_LLM_API\n\n  Client->>OAGW: POST /send (start stream)\n  OAGW->>LLM: invoke embedded library (forward request)\n  LLM->>Provider: HTTP request (SSE passthrough)\n  Provider-->>LLM: SSE events (delta/tool/done/error)\n  LLM-->>OAGW: pass-through SSE events\n  OAGW-->>Client: SSE events streamed to client\n  Client->>OAGW: cancel / close connection\n  OAGW->>LLM: propagate cancellation\n  LLM->>Provider: close HTTP connection (cancel provider stream)\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 2 (Simple) | ⏱️ ~10 minutes\n\n## Possibly related issues\n\n- cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core#627 — Same mini-chat ADRs/DESIGN/PRD additions; likely the same documentation workstream.\n\n## Possibly related PRs\n\n- cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core#322 — Related to OAGW streaming/proxy behavior which aligns with ADR 0002's HTTP + SSE passthrough decision.\n\n## Suggested labels\n\n`spec`\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- nonameffh\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I hopped through docs with eager cheer,  \n> > ADRs and designs all crystal clear,  \n> > Streams that sing and libraries snug,  \n> > Tenants counted with a gentle hug,  \n> > Hop to review — the rabbit's cheer!\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3 | ❌ 1</summary>\n\n### ❌ Failed checks (1 warning)\n\n|        Check name        | Status     | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              