:"write","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","repository_hooks":"write","repository_projects":"write","security_events":"write","statuses":"write","vulnerability_alerts":"read"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3931125754","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/626#issuecomment-3931125754","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/626","id":3931125754,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7qUDf6","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T01:53:41Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T11:26:23Z","body":"> Overall feedback:\r\n> \r\n> 1. The mini-chat must have clear \"no-goals\" list, as we do not want to invest into mini-chat a lot and use normal chat in the future for all the features\r\n> 2. The mini-chat conversation history must be compatible with (or easily migrate'able to) normal chat\r\n> 3. The mini-chat may have shortcuts and hardcoded if/else logic to work with certain environment, e.g. Azure API for conversation or file management\r\n\r\nDid a table-by-table comparison of Mini Chat's DB schema against the \"Big\" Chat engine schema. The two systems are architecturally incompatible in all five core structures:\r\n\r\n1. Content model: TEXT vs JSONB ContentPart[] — different storage format, touches every read/write path\r\nMessage structure: flat chronological list vs tree (parent_message_id + variant_index) — Mini Chat's turn mutation (retry/edit/delete last) depends on linear semantics\r\n\r\n2. Streaming state: dedicated chat_turns table (state machine + idempotency + two-phase quota) vs a single is_complete boolean — cannot be merged without losing streaming reliability\r\n\r\n3. Attachments: rich attachments table (upload lifecycle, cleanup, doc summary, RAG scoping) vs inline file_ids UUID[] — cannot be flattened without losing RAG and cleanup capabilities\r\n\r\n4. Tenant isolation: tenant_id + user_id + Secure ORM vs single client_id — different authorization model entirely\r\n\r\nThe only \"safe\" additive changes (nullable lifecycle_state, metadata JSONB, share_token, visibility flags) would create dead columns that Mini Chat never uses. That's not convergence — it's noise.\r\n\r\nSo I suggest do not maintain separate schemas. These are different products with different architectural trade-offs, not two variants of the same thing.\r\n\r\nProbably DB Schema of Big Chat isn't finished yet.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3931125754/reactions","total_count"