piKey, NoOp)\n+            └── type_provisioning.rs  # GTS type registration\n ```\n \n **Crate Naming Conventions**:\n \n-- Directory names: hyphenated (`oagw-sdk`, `oagw-cp`)\n-- Package names: `cf-` prefix (`cf-oagw-sdk`, `cf-oagw-cp`)\n-- Library names: underscored (`oagw_sdk`, `oagw_cp`)\n+- Directory names: hyphenated (`oagw-sdk`, `oagw`)\n+- Package names: `cf-` prefix (`cf-oagw-sdk`, `cf-oagw`)\n+- Library names: underscored (`oagw_sdk`, `oagw`)\n \n **Plugin Modules** (external):\n \n - Naming: `cf-oagw-plugin-<name>` (e.g., `cf-oagw-plugin-oauth2`, `cf-oagw-plugin-jwt-auth`)\n-- Implement: Plugin traits from `oagw-sdk`\n-- Registered: Via modkit during CP initialization\n+- Implement: `AuthPlugin` trait from `oagw-sdk`\n+- Registered: Via `AuthPluginRegistry` during module initialization\n \n For module structure decisions and trade-offs, see [ADR: Component Architecture](./docs/adr-component-architecture.md).\n ","path":"modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md","commit_id":"04cea814632df97d508624362a221003b4b2f36e","original_commit_id":"9031712ef4dde3cb0703f060c3283df2114d94ec","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@striped-zebra-dev` Acknowledged—thanks for clarifying. I’ll drop the openspec proposal request for this repo. We’ll treat modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md and the ADRs as the source of truth and track future work there.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: striped-zebra-dev\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 624\nFile: modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md:257-305\nTimestamp: 2026-02-17T16:39:13.974Z\nLearning: Repository cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core: This project does not use \"openspec\"; do not request openspec proposals or spec-delta files. For OAGW and related modules, the canonical design sources are modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md and ADRs under modules/system/oagw/docs, with future work tracked in those documents.\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-09T12:27:35.685Z\nLearning: Open `@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md` when creating a new module including new `modules/<name>/...`, SDK pattern, crate layout, and naming conventions\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.158Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/design.md : In `design.md`, include sections: Context (background/constraints/stakeholders), Goals/Non-Goals, Decisions (what and why with alternatives), Risks/Trade-offs, Migration Plan, and Open Questions\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-09T12:27:35.685Z\nLearning: Open `@/docs/modkit_unified_system/README.md` when the task touches ModKit/module architecture including modules layout, `@/lib/modkit*`, plugins, REST wiring, ClientHub, OpenAPI, lifecycle/stateful tasks, SSE, or standardized HTTP errors\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:10.546Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/openspec/changes/*/design.md : Create a `design.md` file only when the change involves cross-cutting changes across multiple services/modules, new architectural patterns, new external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance/migration complexity, or ambiguity requiring technical decisions. Include sections: Context, Goals/Non-Goals, Decisions (with alternatives considered), Risks/Trade-offs, Migration Plan, and Open Questions\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple-user-settings/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:53:52.427Z\nLearning: Use `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` to learn how to create and apply change proposals, spec format and conventions, and project structure and guidelines\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple-user-settings/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:53:52.427Z\nLearning: Always open `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` when the request introduces new capabilities, breaking changes, architecture shifts, or big performance/security work\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:14.414Z\nLearning: Use `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` to learn about how to create and apply change proposals, spec format and conventions, and project structure and guidelines\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:14.414Z\nLearning: Always open `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` when the request mentions planning or proposals (words like proposal, spec, change, plan), introduces new capabilities, breaking changes, architecture shifts, or big performance/security work, or sounds ambiguous\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.158Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/proposal.md : In `proposal.md`, include sections: Why (1-2 sentences on problem/opportunity), What Changes (bullet list with breaking changes marked **BREAKING**), and Impact (affected specs and code)\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:10.546Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/openspec/changes/*/proposal.md : Create a `proposal.md` file that includes: (1) a 'Why' section explaining the problem/opportunity in 1-2 sentences, (2) a 'What Changes' section with bullet points of changes and marking breaking changes as **BREAKING**, and (3) an 'Impact' section listing affected specs and code\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-11T18:25:47.589Z\nLearning: Run `openspec validate [change-id] --strict` and fix all issues before requesting approval; do not start implementation until proposal is reviewed and approved\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T19:58:10.831Z\nLearning: Create change proposals with `proposal.md`, `tasks.md`, optional `design.md`, and delta specs per affected capability in `openspec/changes/[change-id]/specs/`\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.158Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/specs/**/spec.md : Use `## ADDED` for new capabilities that stand alone; use `## MODIFIED` for behavior changes to existing requirements (include full requirement content); use `## REMOVED` for deprecated features; use `## RENAMED` for name-only changes\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T19:55:41.776Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/**/specs/**/*.md : In spec delta files, use ADDED for new orthogonal capabilities, MODIFIED for behavior changes of existing requirements, and RENAMED for name-only changes\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:39:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:39:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817975189","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817975189"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817975189"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817975189/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":257,"original_start_line":257,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":305,"original_line":305,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817227532,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":506,"position":506,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817990769","pull_request_review_id":3815061617,"id":2817990769,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9yBx","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,489 @@\n+use crate::domain::model::{HttpMethod, ListQuery, Route};\n+use crate::domain::repo::{RepositoryError, RouteRepository};\n+use dashmap::DashMap;\n+use modkit_macros::domain_model;\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+/// In-memory route repository backed by `DashMap`.\n+#[domain_model]\n+pub struct InMemoryRouteRepo {\n+    /// Primary store: route_id -> Route.\n+    store: DashMap<Uuid, Route>,\n+    /// Upstream index: upstream_id -> vec of route_ids.\n+    upstream_index: DashMap<Uuid, Vec<Uuid>>,\n+}\n+\n+impl InMemoryRouteRepo {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            store: DashMap::new(),\n+            upstream_index: DashMap::new(),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for InMemoryRouteRepo {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self::new()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait::async_trait]\n+impl RouteRepository for InMemoryRouteRepo {\n+    async fn create(&self, route: Route) -> Result<Route, RepositoryError> {\n+        let route_id = route.id;\n+        let upstream_id = route.upstream_id;\n+\n+        self.store.insert(route_id, route.clone());\n+\n+        // Update upstream index.\n+        self.upstream_index\n+            .entry(upstream_id)\n+            .or_default()\n+            .push(route_id);\n+\n+        Ok(route)\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn get_by_id(&self, tenant_id: Uuid, id: Uuid) -> Result<Route, RepositoryError> {\n+        self.store\n+            .get(&id)\n+            .filter(|r| r.tenant_id == tenant_id)\n+            .map(|r| r.clone())\n+            .ok_or(RepositoryError::NotFound {\n+                entity: \"route\",\n+                id,\n+            })\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn list_by_upstream(\n+        &self,\n+        tenant_id: Uuid,\n+        upstream_id: Uuid,\n+        query: &ListQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<Route>, RepositoryError> {\n+        let route_ids: Vec<Uuid> = self\n+            .upstream_index\n+            .get(&upstream_id)\n+            .map(|ids| ids.clone())\n+            .unwrap_or_default();\n+\n+        let mut routes: Vec<Route> = route_ids\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter_map(|id| {\n+                self.store\n+                    .get(id)\n+                    .filter(|r| r.tenant_id == tenant_id)\n+                    .map(|r| r.clone())\n+            })\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        routes.sort_by_key(|r| r.id);\n+\n+        let skip = query.skip as usize;\n+        let top = query.top as usize;\n+        Ok(routes.into_iter().skip(skip).take(top).collect())\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn find_matching(\n+        &self,\n+        tenant_id: Uuid,\n+        upstream_id: Uuid,\n+        method: &str,\n+        path: &str,\n+    ) -> Result<Route, RepositoryError> {\n+        let route_ids: Vec<Uuid> = self\n+            .upstream_index\n+            .get(&upstream_id)\n+            .map(|ids| ids.clone())\n+            .unwrap_or_default();\n+\n+        let request_method = parse_method(method);\n+\n+        let mut best: Option<Route> = None;\n+        let mut best_path_len = 0;\n+        let mut best_priority = i32::MIN;\n+\n+        for id in &route_ids {\n+            let Some(route_ref) = self.store.get(id) else {\n+                continue;\n+            };\n+            let route = route_ref.value();\n+\n+            // Must match tenant.\n+            if route.tenant_id != tenant_id {\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+            // Must be enabled.\n+            if !route.enabled {\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+            // Must have HTTP match rules.\n+            let Some(http_match) = &route.match_rules.http else {\n+                continue;\n+            };\n+            // Method must match (unknown methods never match).\n+            let Some(req_method) = &request_method else {\n+                continue;\n+            };\n+            if !http_match.methods.contains(req_method) {\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+            // Path must be a prefix match.\n+            if !path.starts_with(&http_match.path) {\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+\n+            let path_len = http_match.path.len();\n+            let priority = route.priority;\n+\n+            // Select by longest path prefix, then highest priority.\n+            if path_len > best_path_len || (path_len == best_path_len && priority > best_priority) {\n+                best_path_len = path_len;\n+                best_priority = priority;\n+                best = Some(route.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        best.ok_or(RepositoryError::NotFound {\n+            entity: \"route\",\n+            id: Uuid::nil(),\n+        })\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn update(&self, route: Route) -> Result<Route, RepositoryError> {\n+        if !self.store.contains_key(&route.id) {\n+            return Err(RepositoryError::NotFound {\n+                entity: \"route\",\n+                id: route.id,\n+            });\n+        }\n+        self.store.insert(route.id, route.clone());\n+        Ok(route)\n+    }","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/storage/route_repo.rs","commit_id":"04cea814632df97d508624362a221003b4b2f36e","original_commit_id":"d1fde6eab875166fb33d01c5d286df0b8c6712ab","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Acknowledged. The in-memory repo is a test/dev scaffold — the production storage layer will use modkit-db's secure ORM which enforces tenant scoping at the query level (WHERE tenant_id = ?). Adding tenant validation to the in-memory update() is a good idea for test correctness. Will address in a follow-up.","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:43:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:43:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817990769","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817990769"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817990769"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817990769/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":155,"original_start_line":155,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":164,"original_line":164,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817019788,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":164,"position":164,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817992161","pull_request_review_id":3815063359,"id":2817992161,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9yXh","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@\n+\"\"\"Standalone mock upstream HTTP server for OAGW E2E tests.\n+\n+Provides endpoints that simulate an upstream service (OpenAI-compatible JSON,\n+SSE streaming, echo, configurable errors). Started as a session-scoped pytest\n+fixture so the OAGW service under test can proxy to it.\n+\"\"\"\n+import asyncio\n+import json\n+import time\n+\n+from aiohttp import web\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Handlers\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+async def handle_health(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    return web.json_response({\"status\": \"ok\"})\n+\n+\n+async def handle_echo(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"Return received headers and body as JSON.\"\"\"\n+    body = await request.read()\n+    headers = {k.lower(): v for k, v in request.headers.items()}\n+    return web.json_response({\n+        \"headers\": headers,\n+        \"body\": body.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\"),\n+    })\n+\n+\n+async def handle_chat_completions(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"OpenAI-compatible chat completion response.\"\"\"\n+    return web.json_response({\n+        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-mock-123\",\n+        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n+        \"created\": 1_234_567_890,\n+        \"model\": \"gpt-4-mock\",\n+        \"choices\": [{\n+            \"index\": 0,\n+            \"message\": {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Hello from mock server\"},\n+            \"finish_reason\": \"stop\",\n+        }],\n+        \"usage\": {\"prompt_tokens\": 10, \"completion_tokens\": 20, \"total_tokens\": 30},\n+    })\n+\n+\n+async def handle_models(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"OpenAI-compatible model list.\"\"\"\n+    return web.json_response({\n+        \"object\": \"list\",\n+        \"data\": [\n+            {\"id\": \"gpt-4\", \"object\": \"model\", \"created\": 1_234_567_890, \"owned_by\": \"openai\"},\n+            {\"id\": \"gpt-3.5-turbo\", \"object\": \"model\", \"created\": 1_234_567_890, \"owned_by\": \"openai\"},\n+        ],\n+    })\n+\n+\n+async def handle_stream_chat_completions(request: web.Request) -> web.StreamResponse:\n+    \"\"\"SSE streaming chat completion.\"\"\"\n+    resp = web.StreamResponse(\n+        status=200,\n+        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"text/event-stream\", \"Cache-Control\": \"no-cache\"},\n+    )\n+    await resp.prepare(request)\n+\n+    words = [\"Hello\", \" from\", \" mock\", \" server\"]\n+    for i, word in enumerate(words):\n+        delta = {}\n+        if i == 0:\n+            delta[\"role\"] = \"assistant\"\n+        delta[\"content\"] = word\n+        chunk = {\n+            \"id\": \"chatcmpl-mock-stream\",\n+            \"object\": \"chat.completion.chunk\",\n+            \"created\": 1_234_567_890,\n+            \"model\": \"gpt-4-mock\",\n+            \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"delta\": delta, \"finish_reason\": None}],\n+        }\n+        await resp.write(f\"data: {json.dumps(chunk)}\\n\\n\".encode())\n+        await asyncio.sleep(0.01)\n+\n+    # Final chunk with finish_reason\n+    final = {\n+        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-mock-stream\",\n+        \"object\": \"chat.completion.chunk\",\n+        \"created\": 1_234_567_890,\n+        \"model\": \"gpt-4-mock\",\n+        \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"delta\": {}, \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"}],\n+    }\n+    await resp.write(f\"data: {json.dumps(final)}\\n\\n\".encode())\n+    await resp.write(b\"data: [DONE]\\n\\n\")\n+    await resp.write_eof()\n+    return resp\n+\n+\n+async def handle_error_code(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"Return a configurable HTTP error status.\"\"\"\n+    code = int(request.match_info[\"code\"])\n+    return web.json_response(\n+        {\"error\": {\"message\": f\"Simulated error {code}\", \"type\": \"server_error\", \"code\": f\"error_{code}\"}},\n+        status=code,\n+    )\n+\n+\n+async def handle_error_timeout(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"Sleep long enough for the gateway proxy timeout to fire.\"\"\"\n+    await asyncio.sleep(30)\n+    return web.Response(text=\"should not reach here\")\n+\n+\n+async def handle_status(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"Return configurable status code.\"\"\"\n+    code = int(request.match_info[\"code\"])\n+    return web.json_response({\"status\": code, \"description\": f\"Status {code}\"}, status=code)\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# App factory\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+def create_app() -> web.Application:\n+    app = web.Application()\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/health\", handle_health)\n+    app.router.add_post(\"/echo\", handle_echo)\n+    app.router.add_post(\"/v1/chat/completions\", handle_chat_completions)\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/v1/models\", handle_models)\n+    app.router.add_post(\"/v1/chat/completions/stream\", handle_stream_chat_completions)\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/error/{code}\", handle_error_code)\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/error/timeout\", handle_error_timeout)\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/status/{code}\", handle_status)\n+    return app\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Server lifecycle (used by conftest.py fixture)\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+class MockUpstreamServer:\n+    \"\"\"Manages the mock upstream lifecycle for pytest fixtures.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def __init__(self, host: str = \"0.0.0.0\", port: int = 19876):\n+        self.host = host\n+        self.port = port\n+        self._runner: web.AppRunner | None = None","path":"testing/e2e/modules/oagw/mock_upstream.py","commit_id":"d1fde6eab875166fb33d01c5d286df0b8c6712ab","original_commit_id":"d1fde6eab875166fb33d01c5d286df0b8c6712ab","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed — default bind changed to 127.0.0.1 in both the MockUpstreamServer constructor and the argparse default.","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:13Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:13Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817992161","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817992161"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817992161"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817992161/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":142,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":145,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817019798,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":145,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817992247","pull_request_review_id":3815063466,"id":2817992247,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9yY3","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@\n pytest>=7.0.0\n httpx>=0.28.0  # Previously 0.23.0 minimum for PYSEC-2022-183 fix\n pytest-asyncio\n+aiohttp>=3.9.0  # Mock upstream server for OAGW E2E tests","path":"testing/e2e/requirements.txt","commit_id":"d1fde6eab875166fb33d01c5d286df0b8c6712ab","original_commit_id":"d1fde6eab875166fb33d01c5d286df0b8c6712ab","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed — bumped aiohttp minimum to >=3.13.3 in requirements.txt. E2E tests pass (29/29).","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:14Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817992247","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817992247"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817992247"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817992247/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":4,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817019806,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817992327","pull_request_review_id":3815063569,"id":2817992327,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9yaH","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,990 @@\n+//! Infrastructure implementation of `TypeProvisioningService` backed by `TypesRegistryClient`.\n+//!\n+//! Queries the types-registry for upstream and route GTS instances registered\n+//! by other modules during `init()`, deserializes their content, and returns\n+//! domain-level provisioned objects for `post_init()` to insert into repos.\n+\n+use std::collections::HashMap;\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use serde::Deserialize;\n+use types_registry_sdk::{ListQuery, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+use crate::domain::error::DomainError;\n+use crate::domain::gts_helpers::{ROUTE_SCHEMA, UPSTREAM_SCHEMA};\n+use crate::domain::model as domain;\n+use crate::domain::type_provisioning::{\n+    ProvisionedRoute, ProvisionedUpstream, TypeProvisioningService,\n+};\n+\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+// Local serde types for GTS entity deserialization.\n+//\n+// These mirror the GTS JSON shape and convert to domain types. They are\n+// intentionally separate from REST DTOs so each can evolve independently.\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+fn default_true() -> bool {\n+    true\n+}\n+\n+fn default_port() -> u16 {\n+    443\n+}\n+\n+fn default_cost() -> u32 {\n+    1\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum Scheme {\n+    Http,\n+    #[default]\n+    Https,\n+    Wss,\n+    Wt,\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct Endpoint {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    scheme: Scheme,\n+    host: String,\n+    #[serde(default = \"default_port\")]\n+    port: u16,\n+}","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/type_provisioning.rs","commit_id":"04cea814632df97d508624362a221003b4b2f36e","original_commit_id":"9031712ef4dde3cb0703f060c3283df2114d94ec","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Valid point — default_port() always returns 443 regardless of scheme. This only affects GTS type provisioning (deserialization from types-registry), not the proxy path. In practice all our upstreams specify explicit ports. Will fix in a follow-up to derive from scheme (443 for https, 80 for http).","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817992327","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817992327"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817992327"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817992327/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":33,"original_start_line":33,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":59,"original_line":59,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817227542,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":59,"position":59,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817992396","pull_request_review_id":3815063675,"id":2817992396,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9ybM","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,990 @@\n+//! Infrastructure implementation of `TypeProvisioningService` backed by `TypesRegistryClient`.\n+//!\n+//! Queries the types-registry for upstream and route GTS instances registered\n+//! by other modules during `init()`, deserializes their content, and returns\n+//! domain-level provisioned objects for `post_init()` to insert into repos.\n+\n+use std::collections::HashMap;\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use serde::Deserialize;\n+use types_registry_sdk::{ListQuery, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+use crate::domain::error::DomainError;\n+use crate::domain::gts_helpers::{ROUTE_SCHEMA, UPSTREAM_SCHEMA};\n+use crate::domain::model as domain;\n+use crate::domain::type_provisioning::{\n+    ProvisionedRoute, ProvisionedUpstream, TypeProvisioningService,\n+};\n+\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+// Local serde types for GTS entity deserialization.\n+//\n+// These mirror the GTS JSON shape and convert to domain types. They are\n+// intentionally separate from REST DTOs so each can evolve independently.\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+fn default_true() -> bool {\n+    true\n+}\n+\n+fn default_port() -> u16 {\n+    443\n+}\n+\n+fn default_cost() -> u32 {\n+    1\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum Scheme {\n+    Http,\n+    #[default]\n+    Https,\n+    Wss,\n+    Wt,\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct Endpoint {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    scheme: Scheme,\n+    host: String,\n+    #[serde(default = \"default_port\")]\n+    port: u16,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct Server {\n+    endpoints: Vec<Endpoint>,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum SharingMode {\n+    #[default]\n+    Private,\n+    Inherit,\n+    Enforce,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct AuthConfig {\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    plugin_type: String,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    sharing: SharingMode,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    config: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum PassthroughMode {\n+    #[default]\n+    None,\n+    Allowlist,\n+    All,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+struct RequestHeaderRules {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    set: HashMap<String, String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    add: HashMap<String, String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    remove: Vec<String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    passthrough: PassthroughMode,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    passthrough_allowlist: Vec<String>,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+struct ResponseHeaderRules {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    set: HashMap<String, String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    add: HashMap<String, String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    remove: Vec<String>,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+struct HeadersConfig {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    request: Option<RequestHeaderRules>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    response: Option<ResponseHeaderRules>,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+struct PluginsConfig {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    sharing: SharingMode,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    items: Vec<String>,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\n+enum RateLimitAlgorithm {\n+    #[default]\n+    TokenBucket,\n+    SlidingWindow,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum Window {\n+    #[default]\n+    Second,\n+    Minute,\n+    Hour,\n+    Day,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct SustainedRate {\n+    rate: u32,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    window: Window,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct BurstConfig {\n+    capacity: u32,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum RateLimitScope {\n+    Global,\n+    #[default]\n+    Tenant,\n+    User,\n+    Ip,\n+    Route,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum RateLimitStrategy {\n+    #[default]\n+    Reject,\n+    Queue,\n+    Degrade,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct RateLimitConfig {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    sharing: SharingMode,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    algorithm: RateLimitAlgorithm,\n+    sustained: SustainedRate,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    burst: Option<BurstConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    scope: RateLimitScope,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    strategy: RateLimitStrategy,\n+    #[serde(default = \"default_cost\")]\n+    cost: u32,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"UPPERCASE\")]\n+enum HttpMethod {\n+    Get,\n+    Post,\n+    Put,\n+    Delete,\n+    Patch,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum PathSuffixMode {\n+    Disabled,\n+    #[default]\n+    Append,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct HttpMatch {\n+    methods: Vec<HttpMethod>,\n+    path: String,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    query_allowlist: Vec<String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    path_suffix_mode: PathSuffixMode,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct GrpcMatch {\n+    service: String,\n+    method: String,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct MatchRules {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    http: Option<HttpMatch>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    grpc: Option<GrpcMatch>,\n+}\n+\n+/// Intermediate serde struct for deserializing upstream GTS entity content.\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct UpstreamPayload {\n+    tenant_id: Uuid,\n+    server: Server,\n+    protocol: String,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    alias: Option<String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    auth: Option<AuthConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    headers: Option<HeadersConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    plugins: Option<PluginsConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    rate_limit: Option<RateLimitConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    tags: Vec<String>,\n+    #[serde(default = \"default_true\")]\n+    enabled: bool,\n+}\n+\n+/// Intermediate serde struct for deserializing route GTS entity content.\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct RoutePayload {\n+    tenant_id: Uuid,\n+    upstream_id: Uuid,\n+    #[serde(rename = \"match\")]\n+    match_rules: MatchRules,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    plugins: Option<PluginsConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    rate_limit: Option<RateLimitConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    tags: Vec<String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    priority: i32,\n+    #[serde(default = \"default_true\")]\n+    enabled: bool,\n+}\n+\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+// From conversions: local payload types → domain types\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+impl From<Scheme> for domain::Scheme {\n+    fn from(v: Scheme) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            Scheme::Http => Self::Http,\n+            Scheme::Https => Self::Https,\n+            Scheme::Wss => Self::Wss,\n+            Scheme::Wt => Self::Wt,\n+            Scheme::Grpc => Self::Grpc,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<Endpoint> for domain::Endpoint {\n+    fn from(v: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            scheme: v.scheme.into(),\n+            host: v.host,\n+            port: v.port,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<Server> for domain::Server {\n+    fn from(v: Server) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            endpoints: v.endpoints.into_iter().map(Into::into).collect(),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<SharingMode> for domain::SharingMode {\n+    fn from(v: SharingMode) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            SharingMode::Private => Self::Private,\n+            SharingMode::Inherit => Self::Inherit,\n+            SharingMode::Enforce => Self::Enforce,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<AuthConfig> for domain::AuthConfig {\n+    fn from(v: AuthConfig) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            plugin_type: v.plugin_type,\n+            sharing: v.sharing.into(),\n+            config: v.config,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<PassthroughMode> for domain::PassthroughMode {\n+    fn from(v: PassthroughMode) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            PassthroughMode::None => Self::None,\n+            PassthroughMode::Allowlist => Self::Allowlist,\n+            PassthroughMode::All => Self::All,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<RequestHeaderRules> for domain::RequestHeaderRules {\n+    fn from(v: RequestHeaderRules) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            set: v.set,\n+            add: v.add,\n+            remove: v.remove,\n+            passthrough: v.passthrough.into(),\n+            passthrough_allowlist: v.passthrough_allowlist,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<ResponseHeaderRules> for domain::ResponseHeaderRules {\n+    fn from(v: ResponseHeaderRules) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            set: v.set,\n+            add: v.add,\n+            remove: v.remove,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<HeadersConfig> for domain::HeadersConfig {\n+    fn from(v: HeadersConfig) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            request: v.request.map(Into::into),\n+            response: v.response.map(Into::into),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<RateLimitAlgorithm> for domain::RateLimitAlgorithm {\n+    fn from(v: RateLimitAlgorithm) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            RateLimitAlgorithm::TokenBucket => Self::TokenBucket,\n+            RateLimitAlgorithm::SlidingWindow => Self::SlidingWindow,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<Window> for domain::Window {\n+    fn from(v: Window) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            Window::Second => Self::Second,\n+            Window::Minute => Self::Minute,\n+            Window::Hour => Self::Hour,\n+            Window::Day => Self::Day,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<SustainedRate> for domain::SustainedRate {\n+    fn from(v: SustainedRate) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            rate: v.rate,\n+            window: v.window.into(),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<BurstConfig> for domain::BurstConfig {\n+    fn from(v: BurstConfig) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            capacity: v.capacity,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<RateLimitScope> for domain::RateLimitScope {\n+    fn from(v: RateLimitScope) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            RateLimitScope::Global => Self::Global,\n+            RateLimitScope::Tenant => Self::Tenant,\n+            RateLimitScope::User => Self::User,\n+            RateLimitScope::Ip => Self::Ip,\n+            RateLimitScope::Route => Self::Route,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<RateLimitStrategy> for domain::RateLimitStrategy {\n+    fn from(v: RateLimitStrategy) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            RateLimitStrategy::Reject => Self::Reject,\n+            RateLimitStrategy::Queue => Self::Queue,\n+            RateLimitStrategy::Degrade => Self::Degrade,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<RateLimitConfig> for domain::RateLimitConfig {\n+    fn from(v: RateLimitConfig) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            sharing: v.sharing.into(),\n+            algorithm: v.algorithm.into(),\n+            sustained: v.sustained.into(),\n+            burst: v.burst.map(Into::into),\n+            scope: v.scope.into(),\n+            strategy: v.strategy.into(),\n+            cost: v.cost,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<PluginsConfig> for domain::PluginsConfig {\n+    fn from(v: PluginsConfig) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            sharing: v.sharing.into(),\n+            items: v.items,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<HttpMethod> for domain::HttpMethod {\n+    fn from(v: HttpMethod) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            HttpMethod::Get => Self::Get,\n+            HttpMethod::Post => Self::Post,\n+            HttpMethod::Put => Self::Put,\n+            HttpMethod::Delete => Self::Delete,\n+            HttpMethod::Patch => Self::Patch,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<PathSuffixMode> for domain::PathSuffixMode {\n+    fn from(v: PathSuffixMode) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            PathSuffixMode::Disabled => Self::Disabled,\n+            PathSuffixMode::Append => Self::Append,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<HttpMatch> for domain::HttpMatch {\n+    fn from(v: HttpMatch) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            methods: v.methods.into_iter().map(Into::into).collect(),\n+            path: v.path,\n+            query_allowlist: v.query_allowlist,\n+            path_suffix_mode: v.path_suffix_mode.into(),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<GrpcMatch> for domain::GrpcMatch {\n+    fn from(v: GrpcMatch) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            service: v.service,\n+            method: v.method,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<MatchRules> for domain::MatchRules {\n+    fn from(v: MatchRules) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            http: v.http.map(Into::into),\n+            grpc: v.grpc.map(Into::into),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<UpstreamPayload> for ProvisionedUpstream {\n+    fn from(p: UpstreamPayload) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            tenant_id: p.tenant_id,\n+            request: domain::CreateUpstreamRequest {\n+                server: p.server.into(),\n+                protocol: p.protocol,\n+                alias: p.alias,\n+                auth: p.auth.map(Into::into),\n+                headers: p.headers.map(Into::into),\n+                plugins: p.plugins.map(Into::into),\n+                rate_limit: p.rate_limit.map(Into::into),\n+                tags: p.tags,\n+                enabled: p.enabled,\n+            },\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<RoutePayload> for ProvisionedRoute {\n+    fn from(p: RoutePayload) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            tenant_id: p.tenant_id,\n+            request: domain::CreateRouteRequest {\n+                upstream_id: p.upstream_id,\n+                match_rules: p.match_rules.into(),\n+                plugins: p.plugins.map(Into::into),\n+                rate_limit: p.rate_limit.map(Into::into),\n+                tags: p.tags,\n+                priority: p.priority,\n+                enabled: p.enabled,\n+            },\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// `TypeProvisioningService` implementation that delegates to `TypesRegistryClient`.\n+pub struct TypeProvisioningServiceImpl {\n+    registry: Arc<dyn TypesRegistryClient>,\n+}\n+\n+impl TypeProvisioningServiceImpl {\n+    pub fn new(registry: Arc<dyn TypesRegistryClient>) -> Self {\n+        Self { registry }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl TypeProvisioningService for TypeProvisioningServiceImpl {\n+    async fn list_upstreams(&self) -> Result<Vec<ProvisionedUpstream>, DomainError> {\n+        let query = ListQuery::new()\n+            .with_pattern(format!(\"{UPSTREAM_SCHEMA}*\"))\n+            .with_is_type(false);\n+\n+        let entities = self\n+            .registry\n+            .list(query)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| DomainError::internal(e.to_string()))?;\n+\n+        let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(entities.len());\n+        for entity in entities {\n+            match serde_json::from_value::<UpstreamPayload>(entity.content.clone()) {\n+                Ok(payload) => {\n+                    result.push(payload.into());\n+                }\n+                Err(e) => {\n+                    tracing::warn!(\n+                        gts_id = %entity.gts_id,\n+                        error = %e,\n+                        \"Skipping upstream: failed to deserialize GTS entity content\"\n+                    );\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(result)\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn list_routes(&self) -> Result<Vec<ProvisionedRoute>, DomainError> {\n+        let query = ListQuery::new()\n+            .with_pattern(format!(\"{ROUTE_SCHEMA}*\"))\n+            .with_is_type(false);\n+\n+        let entities = self\n+            .registry\n+            .list(query)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| DomainError::internal(e.to_string()))?;\n+\n+        let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(entities.len());\n+        for entity in entities {\n+            match serde_json::from_value::<RoutePayload>(entity.content.clone()) {\n+                Ok(payload) => {\n+                    result.push(payload.into());\n+                }\n+                Err(e) => {\n+                    tracing::warn!(\n+                        gts_id = %entity.gts_id,\n+                        error = %e,\n+                        \"Skipping route: failed to deserialize GTS entity content\"\n+                    );\n+                }\n+            }","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/type_provisioning.rs","commit_id":"04cea814632df97d508624362a221003b4b2f36e","original_commit_id":"9031712ef4dde3cb0703f060c3283df2114d94ec","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Valid observation. In practice, route creation via the management API validates match rules before persistence. The GTS provisioning path deserializes what was already validated and stored. Adding a defensive check is reasonable but low priority — the invariant is maintained by the write path.","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817992396","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817992396"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817992396"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817992396/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":590,"original_start_line":590,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":614,"original_line":614,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817227545,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":614,"position":614,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817993751","pull_request_review_id":3815065411,"id":2817993751,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9ywX","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@\n+//! Fluent request builder for integration tests.\n+\n+use axum::body::Body;\n+use http::header::HeaderMap;\n+use http::{HeaderName, HeaderValue, Method};\n+use serde::de::DeserializeOwned;\n+use tower::ServiceExt;\n+\n+use super::body::IntoBody;\n+use super::harness::AppHarness;\n+use super::response::TestResponse;\n+\n+/// Fluent HTTP request builder tied to an [`AppHarness`].\n+pub struct RequestCase<'a> {\n+    harness: &'a AppHarness,\n+    method: Method,\n+    path: String,\n+    headers: HeaderMap,\n+    query: Vec<(String, String)>,\n+    body: Option<Body>,\n+}\n+\n+impl<'a> RequestCase<'a> {\n+    pub(crate) fn new(harness: &'a AppHarness, method: Method, path: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            harness,\n+            method,\n+            path: path.into(),\n+            headers: HeaderMap::new(),\n+            query: Vec::new(),\n+            body: None,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Set the request body. Accepts any type implementing [`IntoBody`]:\n+    /// `Json(&struct)`, `serde_json::Value`, `&str`, `String`, `Bytes`, `Vec<u8>`.\n+    pub fn with_body(mut self, body: impl IntoBody) -> Self {\n+        let (b, ct) = body.into_body();\n+        self.body = Some(b);\n+        if let Some(ct) = ct {\n+            self.headers.insert(http::header::CONTENT_TYPE, ct);\n+        }\n+        self\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Add a request header.\n+    pub fn with_header(\n+        mut self,\n+        name: impl Into<HeaderName>,\n+        value: impl Into<HeaderValue>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        self.headers.insert(name.into(), value.into());\n+        self\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Add a query parameter.\n+    pub fn with_query(mut self, key: impl Into<String>, value: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        self.query.push((key.into(), value.into()));\n+        self\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Send the request and return the collected response.\n+    pub async fn send(self) -> TestResponse {\n+        let uri = if self.query.is_empty() {\n+            self.path\n+        } else {\n+            let qs: Vec<String> = self.query.iter().map(|(k, v)| format!(\"{k}={v}\")).collect();\n+            format!(\"{}?{}\", self.path, qs.join(\"&\"))\n+        };","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/test_support/request.rs","commit_id":"04cea814632df97d508624362a221003b4b2f36e","original_commit_id":"9031712ef4dde3cb0703f060c3283df2114d94ec","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Acknowledged — the test helper uses manual query string construction without URL-encoding. It only matters for query values with special characters, which our current tests don't exercise. Low priority but noted for a follow-up.","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:41Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817993751","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817993751"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817993751"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817993751/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":62,"original_start_line":62,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":69,"original_line":69,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817227548,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":69,"position":69,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817993790","pull_request_review_id":3815065461,"id":2817993790,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9yw-","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,990 @@\n+//! Infrastructure implementation of `TypeProvisioningService` backed by `TypesRegistryClient`.\n+//!\n+//! Queries the types-registry for upstream and route GTS instances registered\n+//! by other modules during `init()`, deserializes their content, and returns\n+//! domain-level provisioned objects for `post_init()` to insert into repos.\n+\n+use std::collections::HashMap;\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use serde::Deserialize;\n+use types_registry_sdk::{ListQuery, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+use crate::domain::error::DomainError;\n+use crate::domain::gts_helpers::{ROUTE_SCHEMA, UPSTREAM_SCHEMA};\n+use crate::domain::model as domain;\n+use crate::domain::type_provisioning::{\n+    ProvisionedRoute, ProvisionedUpstream, TypeProvisioningService,\n+};\n+\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+// Local serde types for GTS entity deserialization.\n+//\n+// These mirror the GTS JSON shape and convert to domain types. They are\n+// intentionally separate from REST DTOs so each can evolve independently.\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+fn default_true() -> bool {\n+    true\n+}\n+\n+fn default_port() -> u16 {\n+    443\n+}\n+\n+fn default_cost() -> u32 {\n+    1\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum Scheme {\n+    Http,\n+    #[default]\n+    Https,\n+    Wss,\n+    Wt,\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct Endpoint {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    scheme: Scheme,\n+    host: String,\n+    #[serde(default = \"default_port\")]\n+    port: u16,\n+}","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/type_provisioning.rs","commit_id":"04cea814632df97d508624362a221003b4b2f36e","original_commit_id":"9031712ef4dde3cb0703f060c3283df2114d94ec","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@striped-zebra-dev`, sounds good! Thank you for acknowledging the concern. Since you're planning to address this in a follow-up, would you like me to create an issue to track it?\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: striped-zebra-dev\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 624\nFile: modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md:257-305\nTimestamp: 2026-02-17T16:39:13.974Z\nLearning: Repository cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core: This project does not use \"openspec\"; do not request openspec proposals or spec-delta files. For OAGW and related modules, the canonical design sources are modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md and ADRs under modules/system/oagw/docs, with future work tracked in those documents.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817993790","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817993790"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817993790"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817993790/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":33,"original_start_line":33,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":59,"original_line":59,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817227542,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":59,"position":59,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817993808","pull_request_review_id":3815065487,"id":2817993808,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9yxQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,990 @@\n+//! Infrastructure implementation of `TypeProvisioningService` backed by `TypesRegistryClient`.\n+//!\n+//! Queries the types-registry for upstream and route GTS instances registered\n+//! by other modules during `init()`, deserializes their content, and returns\n+//! domain-level provisioned objects for `post_init()` to insert into repos.\n+\n+use std::collections::HashMap;\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use serde::Deserialize;\n+use types_registry_sdk::{ListQuery, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+use crate::domain::error::DomainError;\n+use crate::domain::gts_helpers::{ROUTE_SCHEMA, UPSTREAM_SCHEMA};\n+use crate::domain::model as domain;\n+use crate::domain::type_provisioning::{\n+    ProvisionedRoute, ProvisionedUpstream, TypeProvisioningService,\n+};\n+\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+// Local serde types for GTS entity deserialization.\n+//\n+// These mirror the GTS JSON shape and convert to domain types. They are\n+// intentionally separate from REST DTOs so each can evolve independently.\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+fn default_true() -> bool {\n+    true\n+}\n+\n+fn default_port() -> u16 {\n+    443\n+}\n+\n+fn default_cost() -> u32 {\n+    1\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum Scheme {\n+    Http,\n+    #[default]\n+    Https,\n+    Wss,\n+    Wt,\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct Endpoint {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    scheme: Scheme,\n+    host: String,\n+    #[serde(default = \"default_port\")]\n+    port: u16,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct Server {\n+    endpoints: Vec<Endpoint>,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum SharingMode {\n+    #[default]\n+    Private,\n+    Inherit,\n+    Enforce,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct AuthConfig {\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    plugin_type: String,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    sharing: SharingMode,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    config: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum PassthroughMode {\n+    #[default]\n+    None,\n+    Allowlist,\n+    All,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+struct RequestHeaderRules {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    set: HashMap<String, String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    add: HashMap<String, String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    remove: Vec<String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    passthrough: PassthroughMode,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    passthrough_allowlist: Vec<String>,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+struct ResponseHeaderRules {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    set: HashMap<String, String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    add: HashMap<String, String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    remove: Vec<String>,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+struct HeadersConfig {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    request: Option<RequestHeaderRules>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    response: Option<ResponseHeaderRules>,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+struct PluginsConfig {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    sharing: SharingMode,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    items: Vec<String>,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\n+enum RateLimitAlgorithm {\n+    #[default]\n+    TokenBucket,\n+    SlidingWindow,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum Window {\n+    #[default]\n+    Second,\n+    Minute,\n+    Hour,\n+    Day,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct SustainedRate {\n+    rate: u32,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    window: Window,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct BurstConfig {\n+    capacity: u32,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum RateLimitScope {\n+    Global,\n+    #[default]\n+    Tenant,\n+    User,\n+    Ip,\n+    Route,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum RateLimitStrategy {\n+    #[default]\n+    Reject,\n+    Queue,\n+    Degrade,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct RateLimitConfig {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    sharing: SharingMode,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    algorithm: RateLimitAlgorithm,\n+    sustained: SustainedRate,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    burst: Option<BurstConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    scope: RateLimitScope,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    strategy: RateLimitStrategy,\n+    #[serde(default = \"default_cost\")]\n+    cost: u32,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"UPPERCASE\")]\n+enum HttpMethod {\n+    Get,\n+    Post,\n+    Put,\n+    Delete,\n+    Patch,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+enum PathSuffixMode {\n+    Disabled,\n+    #[default]\n+    Append,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct HttpMatch {\n+    methods: Vec<HttpMethod>,\n+    path: String,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    query_allowlist: Vec<String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    path_suffix_mode: PathSuffixMode,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct GrpcMatch {\n+    service: String,\n+    method: String,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct MatchRules {\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    http: Option<HttpMatch>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    grpc: Option<GrpcMatch>,\n+}\n+\n+/// Intermediate serde struct for deserializing upstream GTS entity content.\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct UpstreamPayload {\n+    tenant_id: Uuid,\n+    server: Server,\n+    protocol: String,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    alias: Option<String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    auth: Option<AuthConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    headers: Option<HeadersConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    plugins: Option<PluginsConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    rate_limit: Option<RateLimitConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    tags: Vec<String>,\n+    #[serde(default = \"default_true\")]\n+    enabled: bool,\n+}\n+\n+/// Intermediate serde struct for deserializing route GTS entity content.\n+#[derive(Deserialize)]\n+struct RoutePayload {\n+    tenant_id: Uuid,\n+    upstream_id: Uuid,\n+    #[serde(rename = \"match\")]\n+    match_rules: MatchRules,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    plugins: Option<PluginsConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    rate_limit: Option<RateLimitConfig>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    tags: Vec<String>,\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    priority: i32,\n+    #[serde(default = \"default_true\")]\n+    enabled: bool,\n+}\n+\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+// From conversions: local payload types → domain types\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+impl From<Scheme> for domain::Scheme {\n+    fn from(v: Scheme) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            Scheme::Http => Self::Http,\n+            Scheme::Https => Self::Https,\n+            Scheme::Wss => Self::Wss,\n+            Scheme::Wt => Self::Wt,\n+            Scheme::Grpc => Self::Grpc,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<Endpoint> for domain::Endpoint {\n+    fn from(v: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            scheme: v.scheme.into(),\n+            host: v.host,\n+            port: v.port,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<Server> for domain::Server {\n+    fn from(v: Server) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            endpoints: v.endpoints.into_iter().map(Into::into).collect(),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<SharingMode> for domain::SharingMode {\n+    fn from(v: SharingMode) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            SharingMode::Private => Self::Private,\n+            SharingMode::Inherit => Self::Inherit,\n+            SharingMode::Enforce => Self::Enforce,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<AuthConfig> for domain::AuthConfig {\n+    fn from(v: AuthConfig) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            plugin_type: v.plugin_type,\n+            sharing: v.sharing.into(),\n+            config: v.config,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<PassthroughMode> for domain::PassthroughMode {\n+    fn from(v: PassthroughMode) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            PassthroughMode::None => Self::None,\n+            PassthroughMode::Allowlist => Self::Allowlist,\n+            PassthroughMode::All => Self::All,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<RequestHeaderRules> for domain::RequestHeaderRules {\n+    fn from(v: RequestHeaderRules) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            set: v.set,\n+            add: v.add,\n+            remove: v.remove,\n+            passthrough: v.passthrough.into(),\n+            passthrough_allowlist: v.passthrough_allowlist,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<ResponseHeaderRules> for domain::ResponseHeaderRules {\n+    fn from(v: ResponseHeaderRules) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            set: v.set,\n+            add: v.add,\n+            remove: v.remove,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<HeadersConfig> for domain::HeadersConfig {\n+    fn from(v: HeadersConfig) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            request: v.request.map(Into::into),\n+            response: v.response.map(Into::into),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<RateLimitAlgorithm> for domain::RateLimitAlgorithm {\n+    fn from(v: RateLimitAlgorithm) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            RateLimitAlgorithm::TokenBucket => Self::TokenBucket,\n+            RateLimitAlgorithm::SlidingWindow => Self::SlidingWindow,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<Window> for domain::Window {\n+    fn from(v: Window) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            Window::Second => Self::Second,\n+            Window::Minute => Self::Minute,\n+            Window::Hour => Self::Hour,\n+            Window::Day => Self::Day,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<SustainedRate> for domain::SustainedRate {\n+    fn from(v: SustainedRate) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            rate: v.rate,\n+            window: v.window.into(),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<BurstConfig> for domain::BurstConfig {\n+    fn from(v: BurstConfig) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            capacity: v.capacity,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<RateLimitScope> for domain::RateLimitScope {\n+    fn from(v: RateLimitScope) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            RateLimitScope::Global => Self::Global,\n+            RateLimitScope::Tenant => Self::Tenant,\n+            RateLimitScope::User => Self::User,\n+            RateLimitScope::Ip => Self::Ip,\n+            RateLimitScope::Route => Self::Route,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<RateLimitStrategy> for domain::RateLimitStrategy {\n+    fn from(v: RateLimitStrategy) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            RateLimitStrategy::Reject => Self::Reject,\n+            RateLimitStrategy::Queue => Self::Queue,\n+            RateLimitStrategy::Degrade => Self::Degrade,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<RateLimitConfig> for domain::RateLimitConfig {\n+    fn from(v: RateLimitConfig) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            sharing: v.sharing.into(),\n+            algorithm: v.algorithm.into(),\n+            sustained: v.sustained.into(),\n+            burst: v.burst.map(Into::into),\n+            scope: v.scope.into(),\n+            strategy: v.strategy.into(),\n+            cost: v.cost,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<PluginsConfig> for domain::PluginsConfig {\n+    fn from(v: PluginsConfig) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            sharing: v.sharing.into(),\n+            items: v.items,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<HttpMethod> for domain::HttpMethod {\n+    fn from(v: HttpMethod) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            HttpMethod::Get => Self::Get,\n+            HttpMethod::Post => Self::Post,\n+            HttpMethod::Put => Self::Put,\n+            HttpMethod::Delete => Self::Delete,\n+            HttpMethod::Patch => Self::Patch,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<PathSuffixMode> for domain::PathSuffixMode {\n+    fn from(v: PathSuffixMode) -> Self {\n+        match v {\n+            PathSuffixMode::Disabled => Self::Disabled,\n+            PathSuffixMode::Append => Self::Append,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<HttpMatch> for domain::HttpMatch {\n+    fn from(v: HttpMatch) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            methods: v.methods.into_iter().map(Into::into).collect(),\n+            path: v.path,\n+            query_allowlist: v.query_allowlist,\n+            path_suffix_mode: v.path_suffix_mode.into(),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<GrpcMatch> for domain::GrpcMatch {\n+    fn from(v: GrpcMatch) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            service: v.service,\n+            method: v.method,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<MatchRules> for domain::MatchRules {\n+    fn from(v: MatchRules) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            http: v.http.map(Into::into),\n+            grpc: v.grpc.map(Into::into),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<UpstreamPayload> for ProvisionedUpstream {\n+    fn from(p: UpstreamPayload) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            tenant_id: p.tenant_id,\n+            request: domain::CreateUpstreamRequest {\n+                server: p.server.into(),\n+                protocol: p.protocol,\n+                alias: p.alias,\n+                auth: p.auth.map(Into::into),\n+                headers: p.headers.map(Into::into),\n+                plugins: p.plugins.map(Into::into),\n+                rate_limit: p.rate_limit.map(Into::into),\n+                tags: p.tags,\n+                enabled: p.enabled,\n+            },\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl From<RoutePayload> for ProvisionedRoute {\n+    fn from(p: RoutePayload) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            tenant_id: p.tenant_id,\n+            request: domain::CreateRouteRequest {\n+                upstream_id: p.upstream_id,\n+                match_rules: p.match_rules.into(),\n+                plugins: p.plugins.map(Into::into),\n+                rate_limit: p.rate_limit.map(Into::into),\n+                tags: p.tags,\n+                priority: p.priority,\n+                enabled: p.enabled,\n+            },\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// `TypeProvisioningService` implementation that delegates to `TypesRegistryClient`.\n+pub struct TypeProvisioningServiceImpl {\n+    registry: Arc<dyn TypesRegistryClient>,\n+}\n+\n+impl TypeProvisioningServiceImpl {\n+    pub fn new(registry: Arc<dyn TypesRegistryClient>) -> Self {\n+        Self { registry }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl TypeProvisioningService for TypeProvisioningServiceImpl {\n+    async fn list_upstreams(&self) -> Result<Vec<ProvisionedUpstream>, DomainError> {\n+        let query = ListQuery::new()\n+            .with_pattern(format!(\"{UPSTREAM_SCHEMA}*\"))\n+            .with_is_type(false);\n+\n+        let entities = self\n+            .registry\n+            .list(query)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| DomainError::internal(e.to_string()))?;\n+\n+        let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(entities.len());\n+        for entity in entities {\n+            match serde_json::from_value::<UpstreamPayload>(entity.content.clone()) {\n+                Ok(payload) => {\n+                    result.push(payload.into());\n+                }\n+                Err(e) => {\n+                    tracing::warn!(\n+                        gts_id = %entity.gts_id,\n+                        error = %e,\n+                        \"Skipping upstream: failed to deserialize GTS entity content\"\n+                    );\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(result)\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn list_routes(&self) -> Result<Vec<ProvisionedRoute>, DomainError> {\n+        let query = ListQuery::new()\n+            .with_pattern(format!(\"{ROUTE_SCHEMA}*\"))\n+            .with_is_type(false);\n+\n+        let entities = self\n+            .registry\n+            .list(query)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| DomainError::internal(e.to_string()))?;\n+\n+        let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(entities.len());\n+        for entity in entities {\n+            match serde_json::from_value::<RoutePayload>(entity.content.clone()) {\n+                Ok(payload) => {\n+                    result.push(payload.into());\n+                }\n+                Err(e) => {\n+                    tracing::warn!(\n+                        gts_id = %entity.gts_id,\n+                        error = %e,\n+                        \"Skipping route: failed to deserialize GTS entity content\"\n+                    );\n+                }\n+            }","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/type_provisioning.rs","commit_id":"04cea814632df97d508624362a221003b4b2f36e","original_commit_id":"9031712ef4dde3cb0703f060c3283df2114d94ec","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@striped-zebra-dev`, thank you for the context! That makes sense — if the management API enforces the invariant at write time, the provisioning path can safely assume valid data. The defensive check would add defense-in-depth, but I understand it's not a priority given the current architecture.\n\nIf you'd like to track it for future hardening, I can help add a TODO comment or document the assumption. Otherwise, I'll consider this addressed.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: striped-zebra-dev\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 624\nFile: modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md:257-305\nTimestamp: 2026-02-17T16:39:13.974Z\nLearning: Repository cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core: This project does not use \"openspec\"; do not request openspec proposals or spec-delta files. For OAGW and related modules, the canonical design sources are modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md and ADRs under modules/system/oagw/docs, with future work tracked in those documents.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817993808","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817993808"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817993808"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817993808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":590,"original_start_line":590,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":614,"original_line":614,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817227545,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":614,"position":614,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817993833","pull_request_review_id":3815065521,"id":2817993833,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9yxp","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@\n+\"\"\"Standalone mock upstream HTTP server for OAGW E2E tests.\n+\n+Provides endpoints that simulate an upstream service (OpenAI-compatible JSON,\n+SSE streaming, echo, configurable errors). Started as a session-scoped pytest\n+fixture so the OAGW service under test can proxy to it.\n+\"\"\"\n+import asyncio\n+import json\n+import time\n+\n+from aiohttp import web\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Handlers\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+async def handle_health(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    return web.json_response({\"status\": \"ok\"})\n+\n+\n+async def handle_echo(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"Return received headers and body as JSON.\"\"\"\n+    body = await request.read()\n+    headers = {k.lower(): v for k, v in request.headers.items()}\n+    return web.json_response({\n+        \"headers\": headers,\n+        \"body\": body.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\"),\n+    })\n+\n+\n+async def handle_chat_completions(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"OpenAI-compatible chat completion response.\"\"\"\n+    return web.json_response({\n+        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-mock-123\",\n+        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n+        \"created\": 1_234_567_890,\n+        \"model\": \"gpt-4-mock\",\n+        \"choices\": [{\n+            \"index\": 0,\n+            \"message\": {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Hello from mock server\"},\n+            \"finish_reason\": \"stop\",\n+        }],\n+        \"usage\": {\"prompt_tokens\": 10, \"completion_tokens\": 20, \"total_tokens\": 30},\n+    })\n+\n+\n+async def handle_models(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"OpenAI-compatible model list.\"\"\"\n+    return web.json_response({\n+        \"object\": \"list\",\n+        \"data\": [\n+            {\"id\": \"gpt-4\", \"object\": \"model\", \"created\": 1_234_567_890, \"owned_by\": \"openai\"},\n+            {\"id\": \"gpt-3.5-turbo\", \"object\": \"model\", \"created\": 1_234_567_890, \"owned_by\": \"openai\"},\n+        ],\n+    })\n+\n+\n+async def handle_stream_chat_completions(request: web.Request) -> web.StreamResponse:\n+    \"\"\"SSE streaming chat completion.\"\"\"\n+    resp = web.StreamResponse(\n+        status=200,\n+        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"text/event-stream\", \"Cache-Control\": \"no-cache\"},\n+    )\n+    await resp.prepare(request)\n+\n+    words = [\"Hello\", \" from\", \" mock\", \" server\"]\n+    for i, word in enumerate(words):\n+        delta = {}\n+        if i == 0:\n+            delta[\"role\"] = \"assistant\"\n+        delta[\"content\"] = word\n+        chunk = {\n+            \"id\": \"chatcmpl-mock-stream\",\n+            \"object\": \"chat.completion.chunk\",\n+            \"created\": 1_234_567_890,\n+            \"model\": \"gpt-4-mock\",\n+            \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"delta\": delta, \"finish_reason\": None}],\n+        }\n+        await resp.write(f\"data: {json.dumps(chunk)}\\n\\n\".encode())\n+        await asyncio.sleep(0.01)\n+\n+    # Final chunk with finish_reason\n+    final = {\n+        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-mock-stream\",\n+        \"object\": \"chat.completion.chunk\",\n+        \"created\": 1_234_567_890,\n+        \"model\": \"gpt-4-mock\",\n+        \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"delta\": {}, \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"}],\n+    }\n+    await resp.write(f\"data: {json.dumps(final)}\\n\\n\".encode())\n+    await resp.write(b\"data: [DONE]\\n\\n\")\n+    await resp.write_eof()\n+    return resp\n+\n+\n+async def handle_error_code(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"Return a configurable HTTP error status.\"\"\"\n+    code = int(request.match_info[\"code\"])\n+    return web.json_response(\n+        {\"error\": {\"message\": f\"Simulated error {code}\", \"type\": \"server_error\", \"code\": f\"error_{code}\"}},\n+        status=code,\n+    )\n+\n+\n+async def handle_error_timeout(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"Sleep long enough for the gateway proxy timeout to fire.\"\"\"\n+    await asyncio.sleep(30)\n+    return web.Response(text=\"should not reach here\")\n+\n+\n+async def handle_status(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"Return configurable status code.\"\"\"\n+    code = int(request.match_info[\"code\"])\n+    return web.json_response({\"status\": code, \"description\": f\"Status {code}\"}, status=code)\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# App factory\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+def create_app() -> web.Application:\n+    app = web.Application()\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/health\", handle_health)\n+    app.router.add_post(\"/echo\", handle_echo)\n+    app.router.add_post(\"/v1/chat/completions\", handle_chat_completions)\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/v1/models\", handle_models)\n+    app.router.add_post(\"/v1/chat/completions/stream\", handle_stream_chat_completions)\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/error/{code}\", handle_error_code)\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/error/timeout\", handle_error_timeout)\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/status/{code}\", handle_status)\n+    return app\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Server lifecycle (used by conftest.py fixture)\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+class MockUpstreamServer:\n+    \"\"\"Manages the mock upstream lifecycle for pytest fixtures.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def __init__(self, host: str = \"0.0.0.0\", port: int = 19876):\n+        self.host = host\n+        self.port = port\n+        self._runner: web.AppRunner | None = None","path":"testing/e2e/modules/oagw/mock_upstream.py","commit_id":"d1fde6eab875166fb33d01c5d286df0b8c6712ab","original_commit_id":"d1fde6eab875166fb33d01c5d286df0b8c6712ab","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@striped-zebra-dev`, thank you for addressing the security concern! Binding to `127.0.0.1` by default is the safer choice for test infrastructure, while still allowing explicit overrides when needed in CI/container environments. \n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: striped-zebra-dev\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 624\nFile: modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md:257-305\nTimestamp: 2026-02-17T16:39:13.974Z\nLearning: Repository cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core: This project does not use \"openspec\"; do not request openspec proposals or spec-delta files. For OAGW and related modules, the canonical design sources are modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md and ADRs under modules/system/oagw/docs, with future work tracked in those documents.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:44:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817993833","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817993833"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817993833"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817993833/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":142,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":145,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817019798,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":145,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817995375","pull_request_review_id":3815067515,"id":2817995375,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9zJv","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@\n pytest>=7.0.0\n httpx>=0.28.0  # Previously 0.23.0 minimum for PYSEC-2022-183 fix\n pytest-asyncio\n+aiohttp>=3.9.0  # Mock upstream server for OAGW E2E tests","path":"testing/e2e/requirements.txt","commit_id":"d1fde6eab875166fb33d01c5d286df0b8c6712ab","original_commit_id":"d1fde6eab875166fb33d01c5d286df0b8c6712ab","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@striped-zebra-dev`, excellent! Thank you for promptly addressing the security vulnerabilities by upgrading to `aiohttp>=3.13.3`. Choosing the latest stable release ensures you're protected against all known CVEs, including the recently disclosed CVE-2025-53643. Great to hear all 29 E2E tests are passing! 🎉\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n🐰\n  />  フ\n |  _  _|\n /`ミ _x 彡\n/     |\n/  ヽ   ノ\n│  | | |\n ̄ ̄ ̄ ̄ ̄\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: striped-zebra-dev\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 624\nFile: modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md:257-305\nTimestamp: 2026-02-17T16:39:13.974Z\nLearning: Repository cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core: This project does not use \"openspec\"; do not request openspec proposals or spec-delta files. For OAGW and related modules, the canonical design sources are modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md and ADRs under modules/system/oagw/docs, with future work tracked in those documents.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:45:06Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:45:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817995375","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817995375"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817995375"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817995375/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":4,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817019806,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817995704","pull_request_review_id":3815068078,"id":2817995704,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9zO4","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@\n+//! Fluent request builder for integration tests.\n+\n+use axum::body::Body;\n+use http::header::HeaderMap;\n+use http::{HeaderName, HeaderValue, Method};\n+use serde::de::DeserializeOwned;\n+use tower::ServiceExt;\n+\n+use super::body::IntoBody;\n+use super::harness::AppHarness;\n+use super::response::TestResponse;\n+\n+/// Fluent HTTP request builder tied to an [`AppHarness`].\n+pub struct RequestCase<'a> {\n+    harness: &'a AppHarness,\n+    method: Method,\n+    path: String,\n+    headers: HeaderMap,\n+    query: Vec<(String, String)>,\n+    body: Option<Body>,\n+}\n+\n+impl<'a> RequestCase<'a> {\n+    pub(crate) fn new(harness: &'a AppHarness, method: Method, path: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            harness,\n+            method,\n+            path: path.into(),\n+            headers: HeaderMap::new(),\n+            query: Vec::new(),\n+            body: None,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Set the request body. Accepts any type implementing [`IntoBody`]:\n+    /// `Json(&struct)`, `serde_json::Value`, `&str`, `String`, `Bytes`, `Vec<u8>`.\n+    pub fn with_body(mut self, body: impl IntoBody) -> Self {\n+        let (b, ct) = body.into_body();\n+        self.body = Some(b);\n+        if let Some(ct) = ct {\n+            self.headers.insert(http::header::CONTENT_TYPE, ct);\n+        }\n+        self\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Add a request header.\n+    pub fn with_header(\n+        mut self,\n+        name: impl Into<HeaderName>,\n+        value: impl Into<HeaderValue>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        self.headers.insert(name.into(), value.into());\n+        self\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Add a query parameter.\n+    pub fn with_query(mut self, key: impl Into<String>, value: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        self.query.push((key.into(), value.into()));\n+        self\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Send the request and return the collected response.\n+    pub async fn send(self) -> TestResponse {\n+        let uri = if self.query.is_empty() {\n+            self.path\n+        } else {\n+            let qs: Vec<String> = self.query.iter().map(|(k, v)| format!(\"{k}={v}\")).collect();\n+            format!(\"{}?{}\", self.path, qs.join(\"&\"))\n+        };","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/test_support/request.rs","commit_id":"04cea814632df97d508624362a221003b4b2f36e","original_commit_id":"9031712ef4dde3cb0703f060c3283df2114d94ec","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@striped-zebra-dev`, understood! Since you've noted this for a follow-up, would you like me to create a GitHub issue to track the URL-encoding enhancement for the test helper? I can provide a clear title and description referencing this discussion and the specific code location.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: striped-zebra-dev\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 624\nFile: modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md:257-305\nTimestamp: 2026-02-17T16:39:13.974Z\nLearning: Repository cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core: This project does not use \"openspec\"; do not request openspec proposals or spec-delta files. For OAGW and related modules, the canonical design sources are modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md and ADRs under modules/system/oagw/docs, with future work tracked in those documents.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:45:10Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:45:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817995704","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817995704"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817995704"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817995704/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":62,"original_start_line":62,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":69,"original_line":69,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817227548,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":69,"position":69,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817996263","pull_request_review_id":3815068769,"id":2817996263,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9zXn","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@\n+\"\"\"Pytest configuration and fixtures for OAGW E2E tests.\"\"\"\n+import asyncio\n+import os\n+import threading\n+\n+import httpx\n+import pytest\n+\n+from .mock_upstream import MockUpstreamServer\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Environment-driven fixtures\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+@pytest.fixture\n+def oagw_base_url():\n+    \"\"\"OAGW service base URL.\"\"\"\n+    return os.getenv(\"E2E_OAGW_BASE_URL\", \"http://localhost:8086\")\n+\n+\n+@pytest.fixture\n+def mock_upstream_url():\n+    \"\"\"Mock upstream base URL (must be reachable by the OAGW service).\"\"\"\n+    return os.getenv(\"E2E_MOCK_UPSTREAM_URL\", \"http://127.0.0.1:19876\")\n+\n+\n+@pytest.fixture\n+def tenant_id():\n+    \"\"\"Fixed tenant UUID for test isolation.\"\"\"\n+    return \"aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa\"\n+\n+\n+@pytest.fixture\n+def oagw_headers(tenant_id):\n+    \"\"\"Standard headers for OAGW requests (tenant + optional auth).\"\"\"\n+    headers = {\"x-tenant-id\": tenant_id}\n+    token = os.getenv(\"E2E_AUTH_TOKEN\")\n+    if token:\n+        headers[\"Authorization\"] = f\"Bearer {token}\"\n+    return headers\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Session-scoped mock upstream server\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\n+def mock_upstream():\n+    \"\"\"Start the mock upstream server for the entire test session.\"\"\"\n+    url = os.getenv(\"E2E_MOCK_UPSTREAM_URL\", \"http://127.0.0.1:19876\")\n+\n+    # If a custom URL is set, assume the mock is managed externally.\n+    if os.getenv(\"E2E_MOCK_UPSTREAM_EXTERNAL\"):\n+        yield\n+        return\n+\n+    # Parse port from URL.\n+    port = int(url.rsplit(\":\", 1)[-1].split(\"/\")[0])\n+    server = MockUpstreamServer(host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=port)\n+\n+    # Run the mock server in a background thread with its own event loop\n+    # so it can actually serve requests while tests run.\n+    loop = asyncio.new_event_loop()\n+    loop.run_until_complete(server.start())\n+\n+    thread = threading.Thread(target=loop.run_forever, daemon=True)\n+    thread.start()\n+\n+    yield server\n+\n+    loop.call_soon_threadsafe(loop.stop)\n+    thread.join(timeout=5)\n+    loop.run_until_complete(server.stop())\n+    loop.close()","path":"testing/e2e/modules/oagw/conftest.py","commit_id":"04cea814632df97d508624362a221003b4b2f36e","original_commit_id":"9031712ef4dde3cb0703f060c3283df2114d94ec","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Good catch on the teardown sequence. After loop.stop() + thread.join(), calling loop.run_until_complete() on the stopped loop should still work since the loop is stopped but not closed — run_until_complete restarts it for that coroutine. That said, the pattern is fragile. The server.stop() does runner.cleanup() which is quick. In practice we haven't seen failures here, but will clean up the fixture in a follow-up.","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:45:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:45:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817996263","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817996263"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817996263"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817996263/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":72,"original_start_line":72,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":75,"original_line":75,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2817227553,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":75,"position":75,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817996354","pull_request_review_id":3815068864,"id":2817996354,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n9zZC","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@\n+\"\"\"Standalone mock upstream HTTP server for OAGW E2E tests.\n+\n+Provides endpoints that simulate an upstream service (OpenAI-compatible JSON,\n+SSE streaming, echo, configurable errors). Started as a session-scoped pytest\n+fixture so the OAGW service under test can proxy to it.\n+\"\"\"\n+import asyncio\n+import json\n+import time\n+\n+from aiohttp import web\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Handlers\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+async def handle_health(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    return web.json_response({\"status\": \"ok\"})\n+\n+\n+async def handle_echo(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"Return received headers and body as JSON.\"\"\"\n+    body = await request.read()\n+    headers = {k.lower(): v for k, v in request.headers.items()}\n+    return web.json_response({\n+        \"headers\": headers,\n+        \"body\": body.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\"),\n+    })\n+\n+\n+async def handle_chat_completions(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"OpenAI-compatible chat completion response.\"\"\"\n+    return web.json_response({\n+        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-mock-123\",\n+        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n+        \"created\": 1_234_567_890,\n+        \"model\": \"gpt-4-mock\",\n+        \"choices\": [{\n+            \"index\": 0,\n+            \"message\": {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Hello from mock server\"},\n+            \"finish_reason\": \"stop\",\n+        }],\n+        \"usage\": {\"prompt_tokens\": 10, \"completion_tokens\": 20, \"total_tokens\": 30},\n+    })\n+\n+\n+async def handle_models(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"OpenAI-compatible model list.\"\"\"\n+    return web.json_response({\n+        \"object\": \"list\",\n+        \"data\": [\n+            {\"id\": \"gpt-4\", \"object\": \"model\", \"created\": 1_234_567_890, \"owned_by\": \"openai\"},\n+            {\"id\": \"gpt-3.5-turbo\", \"object\": \"model\", \"created\": 1_234_567_890, \"owned_by\": \"openai\"},\n+        ],\n+    })\n+\n+\n+async def handle_stream_chat_completions(request: web.Request) -> web.StreamResponse:\n+    \"\"\"SSE streaming chat completion.\"\"\"\n+    resp = web.StreamResponse(\n+        status=200,\n+        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"text/event-stream\", \"Cache-Control\": \"no-cache\"},\n+    )\n+    await resp.prepare(request)\n+\n+    words = [\"Hello\", \" from\", \" mock\", \" server\"]\n+    for i, word in enumerate(words):\n+        delta = {}\n+        if i == 0:\n+            delta[\"role\"] = \"assistant\"\n+        delta[\"content\"] = word\n+        chunk = {\n+            \"id\": \"chatcmpl-mock-stream\",\n+            \"object\": \"chat.completion.chunk\",\n+            \"created\": 1_234_567_890,\n+            \"model\": \"gpt-4-mock\",\n+            \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"delta\": delta, \"finish_reason\": None}],\n+        }\n+        await resp.write(f\"data: {json.dumps(chunk)}\\n\\n\".encode())\n+        await asyncio.sleep(0.01)\n+\n+    # Final chunk with finish_reason\n+    final = {\n+        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-mock-stream\",\n+        \"object\": \"chat.completion.chunk\",\n+        \"created\": 1_234_567_890,\n+        \"model\": \"gpt-4-mock\",\n+        \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"delta\": {}, \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"}],\n+    }\n+    await resp.write(f\"data: {json.dumps(final)}\\n\\n\".encode())\n+    await resp.write(b\"data: [DONE]\\n\\n\")\n+    await resp.write_eof()\n+    return resp\n+\n+\n+async def handle_error_code(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"Return a configurable HTTP error status.\"\"\"\n+    code = int(request.match_info[\"code\"])\n+    return web.json_response(\n+        {\"error\": {\"message\": f\"Simulated error {code}\", \"type\": \"server_error\", \"code\": f\"error_{code}\"}},\n+        status=code,\n+    )\n+\n+\n+async def handle_error_timeout(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"Sleep long enough for the gateway proxy timeout to fire.\"\"\"\n+    await asyncio.sleep(30)\n+    return web.Response(text=\"should not reach here\")\n+\n+\n+async def handle_status(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n+    \"\"\"Return configurable status code.\"\"\"\n+    code = int(request.match_info[\"code\"])\n+    return web.json_response({\"status\": code, \"description\": f\"Status {code}\"}, status=code)\n+\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# App factory\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+def create_app() -> web.Application:\n+    app = web.Application()\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/health\", handle_health)\n+    app.router.add_post(\"/echo\", handle_echo)\n+    app.router.add_post(\"/v1/chat/completions\", handle_chat_completions)\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/v1/models\", handle_models)\n+    app.router.add_post(\"/v1/chat/completions/stream\", handle_stream_chat_completions)\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/error/{code}\", handle_error_code)\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/error/timeout\", handle_error_timeout)\n+    app.router.add_get(\"/status/{code}\", handle_status)","path":"testing/e2e/modules/oagw/mock_upstream.py","commit_id":"9031712ef4dde3cb0703f060c3283df2114d94ec","original_commit_id":"9031712ef4dde3cb0703f060c3283df2114d94ec","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Good catch — aiohttp's router matches routes in registration order, so /error/{code} at line 129 will match 'timeout' before the static /error/timeout at line 130 gets a chance. The timeout handler is effectively unreachable. However, the OAGW e2e tests access this via the proxy path /error/timeout which routes through OAGW to the mock upstream using the /error/{code} handler — and since that handler does int(code) on 'timeout', it would raise an error. Looking at the test, it works because the gateway's own timeout fires first (2s < 30s sleep). Will fix the route order anyway.","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:45:19Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:45:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2817996354","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2817996354"},"html":{"href":"https://githu