odules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/src/error.rs\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1526\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Get the test implementation\nsed -n '703,750p' modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/client.rs\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1582\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Get complete ServiceGatewayError enum\ncat modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/src/error.rs\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1526\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Find DomainError definition and NotFound variant\nrg -A 20 \"enum DomainError\" modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1660\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check for usages of DomainError::NotFound to see what entities are passed\nrg -B 2 -A 2 \"DomainError::NotFound\" modules/system/oagw/\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 5732\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Map `DomainError::NotFound` by entity type, not all to `RouteNotFound`.**\n\nAll not-found errors currently map to `RouteNotFound`, even when the missing entity is an upstream. This breaks error semantics for clients—a missing upstream should not be reported as a routing failure. The test at line 703 confirms this: it creates a NotFound error with `entity: \"upstream\"` but expects `RouteNotFound`, which is incorrect.\n\nHowever, the suggested variant names (`UpstreamNotFound`, generic `NotFound`) do not exist in the `ServiceGatewayError` enum. You must either:\n1. Add the necessary variants to `ServiceGatewayError` (e.g., `UpstreamNotFound`, `NotFound`), or\n2. Choose a different mapping strategy using existing variants.\n\nOnce resolved, update the `domain_err_not_found_maps_to_sdk` test to assert the correct error type for each entity.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/client.rs` around lines 202 -\n261, domain_err_to_sdk currently maps all DomainError::NotFound cases to\nServiceGatewayError::RouteNotFound; update the mapping so missing upstreams are\nnot reported as route failures: modify the match arm for DomainError::NotFound\nin function domain_err_to_sdk to inspect the entity string and map \"upstream\" to\nan appropriate existing ServiceGatewayError variant (or add a new variant like\nUpstreamNotFound/NotFound to the ServiceGatewayError enum and use it), then\nupdate the domain_err_not_found_maps_to_sdk test to assert the corrected variant\nfor each entity (ensure you reference DomainError::NotFound { entity, id },\nServiceGatewayError::RouteNotFound and the ServiceGatewayError enum when making\nthe change).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:58:02Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T17:07:15Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2818055389","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818055389"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2818055389"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818055389/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":202,"original_start_line":202,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":262,"original_line":261,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":261,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818055395","pull_request_review_id":3815132047,"id":2818055395,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n-Bzj","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,123 @@\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use crate::domain::credential::CredentialResolver;\n+use crate::domain::plugin::{AuthContext, AuthPlugin, PluginError};\n+use serde::Deserialize;\n+\n+/// Configuration for the API key auth plugin.\n+#[derive(Debug, Deserialize)]\n+struct ApiKeyConfig {\n+    /// Header name to set (e.g. \"Authorization\", \"X-API-Key\").\n+    header: String,\n+    /// Prefix prepended to the secret value (e.g. \"Bearer \").\n+    #[serde(default)]\n+    prefix: String,\n+    /// Secret reference to resolve (e.g. \"cred://openai-key\").\n+    secret_ref: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Auth plugin that resolves a secret reference and injects it as a header value.\n+pub struct ApiKeyAuthPlugin {\n+    credential_resolver: Arc<dyn CredentialResolver>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ApiKeyAuthPlugin {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(credential_resolver: Arc<dyn CredentialResolver>) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            credential_resolver,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait::async_trait]\n+impl AuthPlugin for ApiKeyAuthPlugin {\n+    async fn authenticate(&self, ctx: &mut AuthContext) -> Result<(), PluginError> {\n+        let config: ApiKeyConfig = serde_json::from_value(\n+            serde_json::to_value(&ctx.config)\n+                .map_err(|e| PluginError::Internal(format!(\"invalid apikey auth config: {e}\")))?,\n+        )\n+        .map_err(|e| PluginError::Internal(format!(\"invalid apikey auth config: {e}\")))?;\n+\n+        let secret = self\n+            .credential_resolver\n+            .resolve(&config.secret_ref)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|_| PluginError::SecretNotFound(config.secret_ref.clone()))?;","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/plugin/apikey_auth.rs","commit_id":"04cea814632df97d508624362a221003b4b2f36e","original_