n(\"Bearer \"):]\n+            assert len(secret_value) > 0, \"Resolved secret is empty\"\n+        finally:\n+            await delete_upstream(client, oagw_base_url, oagw_headers, uid)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 Ruff (0.15.1)</summary>\n\n[warning] 12-12: Unused function argument: `mock_upstream`\n\n(ARG001)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@testing/e2e/modules/oagw/test_auth_injection.py` around lines 10 - 69, The\ntest function test_apikey_auth_injects_bearer_header currently accepts an unused\nmock_upstream parameter and can leak upstreams when assertions or requests fail;\nremove mock_upstream from the parameter list and add\n`@pytest.mark.usefixtures`(\"mock_upstream\") above the function, and wrap the body\nthat calls create_upstream, create_route, the proxy post and assertions in a\ntry/finally where delete_upstream(client, oagw_base_url, oagw_headers, uid) is\ncalled in finally (guarding for uid existence) so cleanup runs on all paths;\nkeep create_upstream, create_route and delete_upstream calls intact and preserve\nthe existing skip-on-error logic inside the try block.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-17T16:58:03Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T17:07:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2818055419","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818055419"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#discussion_r2818055419"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api