nd_trip.py` around lines 8 - 11, The\nfixture parameter mock_upstream is unused in\ntest_post_proxy_returns_upstream_response (and the other tests flagged at lines\n36-39, 67-70, 104-107), causing ARG001 lint warnings; add a no-op reference to\nmark it used (e.g., assign it to a dummy variable or call a no-op like _ =\nmock_upstream) at the top of each affected test function (including\ntest_post_proxy_returns_upstream_response) so the fixture is considered used\nwhile preserving its side effects.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/oagw/test_management_lifecycle.py-8-11 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`8-11`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Mark `mock_upstream` as used to satisfy linting.**\n\nThese tests don’t reference the fixture directly, which triggers ARG001 warnings. If it’s only for side effects, add a no-op reference.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Example (apply similarly to other tests)</summary>\n\n```diff\n async def test_create_minimal_upstream_returns_201(\n     oagw_base_url, oagw_headers, mock_upstream_url, mock_upstream,\n ):\n     \"\"\"POST /oagw/v1/upstreams with minimal fields returns 201.\"\"\"\n+    _ = mock_upstream\n     alias = unique_alias(\"mgmt-create\")\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 28-31, 52-55, 76-79, 105-108, 131-134, 152-155, 183-186\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@testing/e2e/modules/oagw/test_management_lifecycle.py` around lines 8 - 11,\nThe test functions (e.g., test_create_minimal_upstream_returns_201) accept the\nmock_upstream fixture but never reference it, causing ARG001; fix by adding a\nno-op reference to the fixture at the top of each affected test (for example: _\n= mock_upstream or bool(mock_upstream)) so the fixture is marked used while\nkeeping the side-effect behavior intact; apply the same change to all other\ntests that list mock_upstream as a parameter.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/oagw/test_error_handling.py-101-122 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`101-122`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Ensure cleanup runs even on early exit and fail unexpected statuses.**\n\nThe timeout test has early-exit paths that bypass `delete_upstream`, and the `else: pass` branch lets unexpected statuses succeed silently. Consider wrapping the request logic in `try/finally` and failing on unexpected statuses so cleanup always runs.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        try:\n-            resp = await client.get(\n-                f\"{oagw_base_url}/oagw/v1/proxy/{alias}/error/timeout\",\n-                headers=oagw_headers,\n-            )\n-        except httpx.ReadTimeout:\n-            await delete_upstream(client, oagw_base_url, oagw_headers, uid)\n-            pytest.skip(\"OAGW did not return within 30s — timeout not enforced at gateway level\")\n-            return\n-\n-        if resp.status_code == 504:\n-            # Verify error source header if present; some builds may not set it.\n-            error_source = resp.headers.get(\"x-oagw-error-source\")\n-            if error_source is not None:\n-                assert error_source == \"gateway\"\n-        elif resp.status_code == 200:\n-            pytest.skip(\"OAGW returned 200 — timeout guard may not be configured\")\n-        else:\n-            # Accept any response but log it.\n-            pass\n-\n-        await delete_upstream(client, oagw_base_url, oagw_headers, uid)\n+        try:\n+            resp = await client.get(\n+                f\"{oagw_base_url}/oagw/v1/proxy/{alias}/error/timeout\",\n+                headers=oagw_headers,\n+            )\n+\n+            if resp.status_code == 504:\n+                # Verify error source header if present; some builds may not set it.\n+                error_source = resp.headers.get(\"x-oagw-error-source\")\n+                if error_source is not None:\n+                    assert error_source == \"gateway\"\n+            elif resp.status_code == 200:\n+                pytest.skip(\"OAGW returned 200 — timeout guard may not be configured\")\n+            else:\n+                raise AssertionError(\n+                    f\"Unexpected status from timeout test: {resp.status_code} {resp.text[:500]}\"\n+                )\n+        except httpx.ReadTimeout:\n+            pytest.skip(\n+                \"OAGW did not return within 30s — timeout not enforced at gateway level\"\n+            )\n+        finally:\n+            await delete_upstream(client, oagw_base_url, oagw_headers, uid)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@testing/e2e/modules/oagw/test_error_handling.py` around lines 101 - 122, The\ntest currently can skip or return before calling delete_upstream and lets\nunexpected statuses pass silently; wrap the request/response logic (the\nclient.get call and subsequent status handling) in a try/finally so\ndelete_upstream(client, oagw_base_url, oagw_headers, uid) is always executed in\nthe finally block, and on httpx.ReadTimeout still perform delete_upstream before\ncalling pytest.skip; also replace the loose \"else: pass\" with an explicit\nfailure (e.g., pytest.fail or an assert) to fail the test for unexpected\nresp.status_code values—look for the client.get call and the delete_upstream\ninvocation to apply these changes.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/plugin/registry.rs-33-37 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`33-37`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Use a more semantically appropriate error for unknown plugins.**\n\nThe code maps \"unknown plugin\" to `PluginError::Internal`, which maps to `DomainError::AuthenticationFailed` (401 UNAUTHORIZED). However, an unknown plugin is a configuration/setup issue, not an authentication failure. Consider using `PluginError::Rejected` instead (which maps to `DomainError::Validation` and 400 BAD_REQUEST), or introduce a dedicated error variant in `PluginError` if a different status code is needed.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/plugin/registry.rs` around lines 33 - 37,\nThe resolve method currently returns PluginError::Internal for missing plugins\nwhich incorrectly maps to AuthenticationFailed; update the error to a more\nappropriate variant by returning PluginError::Rejected (or add a new PluginError\nvariant like NotFound/UnknownPlugin if you need a different status) in the\nfailure branch of resolve so the unknown plugin case maps to a\nvalidation/configuration error; adjust the ok_or_else closure that constructs\nthe error (and the error message \"unknown auth plugin: {plugin_id}\") to use the\nchosen PluginError variant.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/oagw/oagw/tests/management_api_test.rs-223-260 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`223-260`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Pagination test assumes deterministic ordering.**  \nIf ordering isn’t guaranteed, offset-based assertions can be flaky; consider asserting only count or enforcing a deterministic order in the API/test setup.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/oagw/tests/management_api_test.rs` around lines 223 -\n260, The test list_upstreams_with_pagination assumes a deterministic ordering\nwhich can make offset assertions flaky; update the test in\nlist_upstreams_with_pagination to avoid relying on ordering: either request a\ndeterministic order from the API (e.g., add a sort/order query when calling\nh.api_v1().list_upstreams()) or change the assertion to only verify the page\nsize and that the returned items contain the expected upstream identifiers\n(e.g., check arr.len() == 2 and that the set of aliases/endpoints from the\nresponse is a subset of the created upstreams via h.facade().create_upstream\ncalls) so the test no longer depends on order.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/request_builder.rs-28-32 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`28-32`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Ensure IPv6 literal hosts are bracketed when forming `host:port`.**\n\nIf `endpoint.host` is an IPv6 literal (contains `:`), `format!(\"{host}:{port}\")` yields an invalid authority. Wrap IPv6 literals in `[]` before adding the port.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested adjustment</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    let host_port = if is_default_port(scheme, endpoint.port) {\n-        endpoint.host.clone()\n-    } else {\n-        format!(\"{}:{}\", endpoint.host, endpoint.port)\n-    };\n+    let host = if endpoint.host.contains(':') && !endpoint.host.starts_with('[') {\n+        format!(\"[{}]\", endpoint.host)\n+    } else {\n+        endpoint.host.clone()\n+    };\n+    let host_port = if is_default_port(scheme, endpoint.port) {\n+        host\n+    } else {\n+        format!(\"{host}:{}\", endpoint.port)\n+    };\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/request_builder.rs` around lines 28\n- 32, host_port construction currently formats endpoint.host and port directly,\nwhich breaks IPv6 literal authorities; modify the logic in the host_port binding\n(used alongside is_default_port and endpoint.port/endpoint.host) to detect IPv6\nliterals (e.g., if endpoint.host contains ':' and is not already surrounded by\n'[' and ']') and wrap the host in brackets before appending \":port\"; keep the\nexisting branch for default ports unchanged and ensure you don't double-bracket\nalready-bracketed hosts.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/plugin/apikey_auth.rs-42-46 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`42-46`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Preserve resolver error semantics instead of collapsing to `SecretNotFound`.**\n\n`CredentialResolver::resolve` can fail for reasons beyond missing secrets; mapping all failures to `SecretNotFound` hides internal resolver failures and misleads callers. Consider matching on the error and mapping non-`NotFound` cases to `PluginError::Internal` (or a distinct failure).\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested mapping</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        let secret = self\n-            .credential_resolver\n-            .resolve(&config.secret_ref)\n-            .await\n-            .map_err(|_| PluginError::SecretNotFound(config.secret_ref.clone()))?;\n+        let secret = self\n+            .credential_resolver\n+            .resolve(&config.secret_ref)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| match e {\n+                crate::domain::credential::CredentialError::NotFound(_) => {\n+                    PluginError::SecretNotFound(config.secret_ref.clone())\n+                }\n+                other => PluginError::Internal(format!(\n+                    \"credential resolution failed for {}: {other}\",\n+                    config.secret_ref\n+                )),\n+            })?;\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/plugin/apikey_auth.rs` around lines 42 -\n46, The current call to\nself.credential_resolver.resolve(&config.secret_ref).await maps all errors to\nPluginError::SecretNotFound which hides other resolver failures; update the\nerror handling in the apikey_auth code to match on the resolver error instead of\nunconditionally mapping: if the resolver returns a NotFound variant return\nPluginError::SecretNotFound(config.secret_ref.clone()), otherwise map other\nerrors to PluginError::Internal (or another distinct variant) preserving the\noriginal error details (e.g., include or wrap the resolver error) so callers can\ndistinguish missing secrets from internal resolver failures; locate this change\naround the resolve call on self.credential_resolver and adjust the map_err usage\naccordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/oagw/conftest.py-86-94 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`86-94`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Address static analysis hints for unused variable and broad exception.**\n\n1. The `resp` variable is assigned but never used - prefix with `_` to indicate intentional discard.\n2. The broad `except Exception: pass` silently swallows errors that might be useful for debugging.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n `@pytest.fixture`(scope=\"session\", autouse=True)\n def _check_oagw_reachable():\n     \"\"\"Skip all OAGW tests if the service is not reachable.\"\"\"\n     url = os.getenv(\"E2E_OAGW_BASE_URL\", \"http://localhost:8086\")\n     try:\n-        resp = httpx.get(f\"{url}/oagw/v1/upstreams\", timeout=5.0,\n-                         headers={\"x-tenant-id\": \"aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa\"})\n+        _resp = httpx.get(f\"{url}/oagw/v1/upstreams\", timeout=5.0,\n+                          headers={\"x-tenant-id\": \"aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa\"})\n         # Any response (even 401/403) means the service is up.\n     except httpx.ConnectError:\n         pytest.skip(f\"OAGW service not running at {url}\", allow_module_level=True)\n-    except Exception:\n-        # Timeout or other transient error — still try to run tests.\n-        pass\n+    except Exception as e:\n+        # Timeout or other transient error — log but still try to run tests.\n+        import warnings\n+        warnings.warn(f\"OAGW reachability check encountered: {e}\")\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@testing/e2e/modules/oagw/conftest.py` around lines 86 - 94, The health-check\nassigns resp from httpx.get but never uses it and catches Exception too broadly;\nrename resp to _resp to mark it intentionally unused and tighten the broad\nexcept by catching only httpx.ReadTimeout and httpx.RequestError (or other\nrelevant httpx transient exceptions) so we don't silently swallow unexpected\nerrors; keep the pytest.skip for httpx.ConnectError and let other unexpected\nexceptions propagate (or re-raise after logging) to aid debugging; update the\ntry/except around httpx.get accordingly (referencing httpx.get, resp/_resp,\npytest.skip).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/client.rs-200-204 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`200-204`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**`NotFound` error maps to `RouteNotFound` regardless of entity type.**\n\n`DomainError::NotFound` for any entity (upstream, route, etc.) maps to `ServiceGatewayError::RouteNotFound`. This loses semantic information and could confuse SDK consumers when an upstream is not found but the error says \"RouteNotFound\".\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested improvement</summary>\n\nConsider adding a more generic `NotFound` variant to `ServiceGatewayError`, or use different SDK error variants based on the entity type:\n\n```diff\n fn domain_err_to_sdk(err: DomainError) -> ServiceGatewayError {\n     match err {\n-        DomainError::NotFound { entity, id } => ServiceGatewayError::RouteNotFound {\n-            instance: format!(\"{entity}/{id}\"),\n-        },\n+        DomainError::NotFound { entity, id } => ServiceGatewayError::NotFound {\n+            entity: entity.to_string(),\n+            instance: format!(\"{entity}/{id}\"),\n+        },\n```\n\nThis would require adding a `NotFound` variant to `ServiceGatewayError` in the SDK.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/client.rs` around lines 200 -\n204, The mapping in domain_err_to_sdk currently converts any\nDomainError::NotFound { entity, id } into ServiceGatewayError::RouteNotFound\nwhich loses entity context; update domain_err_to_sdk to map NotFound errors to a\nnew generic ServiceGatewayError::NotFound { entity, id } (or to distinct\nvariants per entity) and add the corresponding NotFound variant to the\nServiceGatewayError enum so SDK callers receive accurate not-found semantics\ninstead of always RouteNotFound.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management.rs-149-157 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`149-157`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Cascade delete silently ignores errors.**\n\nThe `let _ = self.routes.delete_by_upstream(...)` pattern discards any error from the cascade delete operation. If the route deletion fails (e.g., due to a repository issue), the upstream will still be deleted, leaving orphaned routes in an inconsistent state.\n\nConsider logging the error or propagating it to maintain data consistency.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested improvement</summary>\n\n```diff\n     async fn delete_upstream(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, id: Uuid) -> Result<(), DomainError> {\n         let tenant_id = ctx.tenant_id();\n         // Cascade delete routes.\n-        let _ = self.routes.delete_by_upstream(tenant_id, id).await;\n+        if let Err(e) = self.routes.delete_by_upstream(tenant_id, id).await {\n+            tracing::warn!(\n+                upstream_id = %id,\n+                tenant_id = %tenant_id,\n+                error = %e,\n+                \"Failed to cascade delete routes for upstream\"\n+            );\n+        }\n         self.upstreams\n             .delete(tenant_id, id)\n             .await\n             .map_err(|_| DomainError::not_found(\"upstream\", id))\n     }\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management.rs` around lines 149\n- 157, The delete_upstream function currently ignores errors from\nself.routes.delete_by_upstream(...).await which can leave orphaned routes;\nchange it to handle failures instead of discarding them—call\nself.routes.delete_by_upstream(tenant_id, id).await and either propagate the\nerror (using ? or map_err to a DomainError) or log it and return an appropriate\nDomainError before calling self.upstreams.delete(...).await; update the code\npaths around delete_upstream, routes.delete_by_upstream, and the subsequent\nself.upstreams.delete call so route-deletion failures stop the upstream deletion\n(or are at least logged and returned).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/module.rs-70-73 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`70-73`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Consider redacting credential identifiers in logs.**\n\nLogging the full `secret_ref` value could expose sensitive information about credential naming schemes or internal identifiers. Consider logging only a truncated or hashed version, or omitting it entirely in production.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested improvement</summary>\n\n```diff\n         for (secret_ref, value) in &cfg.credentials {\n-            info!(\"Seeding credential: {secret_ref}\");\n+            info!(\"Seeding credential (count: {})\", cfg.credentials.len());\n             cred_resolver.set(secret_ref.clone(), value.clone());\n         }\n```\n\nOr log only once with the count instead of per-credential.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/module.rs` around lines 70 - 73, The log prints\nthe full secret_ref when seeding credentials (in the loop over cfg.credentials\nwhere info! is called and cred_resolver.set is used), which may leak sensitive\nidentifiers; change the logging so it does not emit full secret names—either\nremove the per-credential info! line, replace it with a redacted/truncated or\nhashed version of secret_ref (e.g., show first/last N chars or a short hash)\nbefore logging, or instead log a single summary line with the total count of\ncredentials seeded after the loop; update the code paths around cfg.credentials,\ninfo!, and cred_resolver.set accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#pullrequestreview-3813938351","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/624#pullrequestreview-3813938351"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/624"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-17T13:22:42Z","commit_id":"d1fde6eab875166fb33d01c5d286df0b8c6712ab"},{"id":3814159489,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7jV3SB","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/f